WEBVTT

01:35.804 --> 01:38.515
BASED ON THE TRUE STORY OF GO PLAYERS
CHO HOON-HYUN AND LEE CHANG-HO

01:38.598 --> 01:41.434
ALL CHARACTERS AND EVENTS
MAY DIFFER FROM REAL-LIFE COUNTERPARTS

01:42.727 --> 01:45.730
THE YING SHIBEI WORLD GO CHAMPIONSHIP
WAS HELD IN THE 1980S

01:45.814 --> 01:47.899
A SINGLE SPOT WAS GIVEN TO KOREA,
AN UNDERDOG COUNTRY

01:47.982 --> 01:50.401
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN
ADVANCED TO THE FINAL AGAINST EXPECTATIONS

01:50.485 --> 01:52.821
HIS OPPONENT, KNOWN AS
"THE BLACK BEAR OF THE CONTINENT,"

01:52.904 --> 01:54.906
WON THE CHINA-JAPAN SUPER LEAGUE
11 CONSECUTIVE TIMES

01:54.989 --> 01:56.282
AND WAS THE WORLD'S BEST PLAYER

01:57.492 --> 02:02.038
The final of the first Ying
Shibei World Professional Go Championship

02:02.122 --> 02:04.415
will be held in Singapore today.

02:04.499 --> 02:08.336
Korea's Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan
and China's Nie Weiping 9-dan,

02:08.419 --> 02:10.380
tying at two wins, two losses each,

02:10.463 --> 02:12.423
will fight in this match of the century

02:12.507 --> 02:15.343
to become king
of the international Go scene.

02:15.426 --> 02:18.096
White has won
in all the previous matches played,

02:18.179 --> 02:22.308
so there is great interest already in
who will play white in the final match.

02:22.392 --> 02:23.935
Champion Cho!

02:24.018 --> 02:25.812
Are you going
to attack fiercely?

02:25.895 --> 02:26.729
Mr. Cho!

02:26.813 --> 02:29.399
What have you done
to prepare for the match today?

02:29.482 --> 02:31.276
Sir!

02:33.069 --> 02:35.738
-Champion Cho!
-Nie Weiping!

02:35.822 --> 02:38.366
How do you feel now?
Piss off to Korea!

02:38.449 --> 02:40.076
Nie Weiping! Nie Weiping!

02:40.160 --> 02:43.830
China will definitely win!
China will definitely win!

02:43.913 --> 02:45.915
MATCH VENUE
STAMFORD HOTEL, SINGAPORE

02:56.968 --> 02:58.803
Nie Weiping 9-dan, white.

02:59.804 --> 03:01.723
Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan, black.

03:17.155 --> 03:18.615
Let the match begin.

03:20.325 --> 03:22.952
THE FIRST YING SHIBEI
WORLD GO CHAMPIONSHIP FINAL, LAST ROUND

03:23.036 --> 03:26.039
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS NIE WEIPING 9-DAN

03:53.816 --> 03:58.696
THE MATCH

03:58.780 --> 04:03.284
Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan has ascended
to the top of the international Go scene.

04:03.368 --> 04:05.161
Cho 9-dan defeated Japan,

04:05.245 --> 04:07.413
who has boasted to be the center
of the Go scene,

04:07.497 --> 04:10.375
and also defeated China,
where Go first originated.

04:11.000 --> 04:12.543
His victory excitingly proves

04:12.627 --> 04:15.588
that the quality of Korea's Go
is at the top of the world.

04:16.172 --> 04:20.885
Right now, well, perhaps I'd not even lose
to the supreme god of Go himself.

04:21.886 --> 04:24.514
Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan,
the Go world champion,

04:24.597 --> 04:26.057
returned to Korea today,

04:26.140 --> 04:28.851
participating in a car parade
from Gimpo Airport

04:28.935 --> 04:31.354
to the Korea Baduk Association
in Jongno 2-ga.

04:31.437 --> 04:33.147
The government
awarded Cho 9-dan

04:33.231 --> 04:35.149
with the Eungwan Order of Culture Merit

04:35.233 --> 04:38.736
for improving the prestige of Korea's Go
throughout the world.

04:40.196 --> 04:44.117
FIVE MONTHS LATER

04:44.200 --> 04:48.204
ONE-ON-MANY TEACHING MATCH
WITH PROFESSIONAL GO PLAYERS

04:48.288 --> 04:49.289
3-DAN CHEON SEUNG-PIL

04:53.167 --> 04:54.752
The boy's amazing.

04:54.836 --> 04:57.422
He solved the life-and-death problem.

04:57.505 --> 04:59.048
-Huh?
-Huh? Right?

04:59.132 --> 05:01.092
-Earlier…
-Hey, hey. Hey, go.

05:02.593 --> 05:03.469
-Okay.
-Hmm?

05:03.553 --> 05:04.762
-Let's go.
-Uh-huh.

05:04.846 --> 05:08.474
Hey, you're in a tight spot,
Pro Cheon.

05:08.558 --> 05:10.184
He's giving you a hard time, huh?

05:10.268 --> 05:12.854
This kid's a Go prodigy in Jeonju.

05:12.937 --> 05:15.189
He's been playing
for less than half a year.

05:15.273 --> 05:18.359
Right, I heard there's no one
who could beat him in Jeonju…

05:18.443 --> 05:21.112
-No, in Jeollanam-do, right? Ha!
-He really must be a prodigy.

05:21.195 --> 05:23.323
I think it's over. Wanna stop?

05:24.907 --> 05:25.950
Just wait.

05:29.620 --> 05:30.788
It's not over yet.

05:30.872 --> 05:31.789
What?

05:33.124 --> 05:35.501
It's over. It's obvious.

05:35.585 --> 05:37.420
Mind if I step in for him?

05:39.380 --> 05:41.716
This is it!

05:56.272 --> 05:57.857
Oh, it's an atari.

05:57.940 --> 05:59.817
ATARI: OPPONENT'S STONE
CAPTURED ON THE NEXT MOVE

05:59.901 --> 06:01.652
Looks like
he's been hit really hard.

06:01.736 --> 06:03.237
Should we call it a tie and stop here?

06:11.162 --> 06:13.581
Champion Cho is Korea's best.
I can't believe it!

06:13.664 --> 06:15.625
Wow, he is amazing.

06:15.708 --> 06:17.502
He's champion for a reason.

06:18.044 --> 06:20.880
It's much harder to win
when you're given the advantage.

06:24.258 --> 06:26.636
You stepped in
when I was going easy.

06:26.719 --> 06:28.429
Hey, wait! Play another one!

06:28.513 --> 06:29.972
Oh, what are you doing?

06:30.056 --> 06:32.433
Hey, you little brat, don't be rude.

06:32.517 --> 06:33.893
Go play over there.

06:33.976 --> 06:36.938
Ugh! You go with the amateurs.

06:37.021 --> 06:38.523
Come on, one more round.

06:38.606 --> 06:40.817
I'll beat you if we play another round.

06:42.235 --> 06:43.403
What's your name, boy?

06:44.695 --> 06:45.988
Chang-ho.

06:46.072 --> 06:46.948
Lee Chang-ho.

06:49.617 --> 06:50.910
Come here. Sit back down.

06:52.745 --> 06:56.332
Chang-ho. Good at life-and-death problems.

06:56.416 --> 06:58.167
LIFE-AND-DEATH: A PLAYER
CAN SAVE THEIR STONES

06:58.251 --> 07:00.420
OR KILL THE OPPONENT'S STONES

07:03.506 --> 07:04.799
Find the black's lifeline.

07:04.882 --> 07:06.676
LIFELINE: A PATH
WHERE STONES CAN ESCAPE ALIVE

07:06.759 --> 07:08.511
This problem,
solve it and we'll play again.

07:08.594 --> 07:10.054
Are you sure about that?

07:10.763 --> 07:12.181
You have to keep your word.

07:12.932 --> 07:14.725
You know, you're not allowed
to take it back.

07:16.018 --> 07:18.271
He's a Lee from Gyeongju too.

07:18.354 --> 07:20.273
A family elder kept talking about him,

07:20.356 --> 07:23.025
so I told him to bring the boy by.

07:23.734 --> 07:25.570
Well, he's good for a kid.

07:28.364 --> 07:30.867
That little kid has quite a temper,
doesn't he?

07:30.950 --> 07:33.953
-So he's your nephew?
-Nah, my first time seeing him too.

07:34.036 --> 07:38.166
The family tree's all messed up
so, he's actually a generation above.

07:38.249 --> 07:41.085
Looks like I'll be taking care
of a young uncle instead.

07:42.795 --> 07:43.880
Your handicap?

07:45.965 --> 07:48.259
Wow. Played a pro
at only a disadvantage of four?

07:48.342 --> 07:51.554
THE NUMBER OF STONES THAT CORRESPONDS
TO A DIFFERENCE IN PLAYERS' STRENGTH

07:51.637 --> 07:53.556
Black? Not white?
Sure you didn't make a mistake?

07:53.639 --> 07:55.475
Mistake? Really?

07:56.058 --> 07:58.019
Why did you give him
an unsolvable problem?

07:58.102 --> 07:59.187
Just to confuse him, huh?

07:59.770 --> 08:01.397
Go problems don't have answers.

08:02.565 --> 08:04.233
I've never seen a play like his.

08:04.817 --> 08:07.778
His haengma and opening are all mixed-up…

08:07.862 --> 08:09.113
THE DIRECTION OR SHAPE OF STONES

08:09.197 --> 08:10.072
…but oddly powerful.

08:10.156 --> 08:11.991
OPENING TACTIC FOR THE GAME'S ADVANTAGE

08:20.458 --> 08:21.375
Ah.

08:24.337 --> 08:25.463
Is it solved?

08:25.546 --> 08:27.131
He can do this.

08:27.215 --> 08:30.426
-Bend and push.
-No, no, no, right here.

08:30.510 --> 08:32.678
-There, I mean--
-Oh, come on.

08:32.762 --> 08:34.388
Ugh, what are you doing?

08:34.472 --> 08:37.767
I told you I had to really
concentrate a lot today.

08:38.267 --> 08:40.603
Stop staring at me,
or nothing will get done.

08:40.686 --> 08:42.438
Yes, I hear you.

08:42.522 --> 08:44.774
My grandson has important work,

08:44.857 --> 08:48.361
so let's step out and have a drink.
It'll be on me.

08:48.444 --> 08:50.029
-My treat, come on.
-I'm in trouble.

08:50.112 --> 08:52.740
If I drink during the day,
I know I'm going to pass out again.

08:52.823 --> 08:55.910
Yeah.
This guy can't even hold his milk--

08:55.993 --> 08:59.413
What about your homework?
You're concentrating on one thing?

09:07.213 --> 09:10.591
Third generation, only-son,
adored by his grandfather.

09:11.217 --> 09:14.845
Humor him and say the boy's good,
that he shows talent.

09:14.929 --> 09:16.806
I'll take care of all the rest.

09:19.809 --> 09:21.644
Ah!

09:22.311 --> 09:27.525
Amazing, huh? His playing
has a lot of maturity!

09:27.608 --> 09:29.569
-I'm number one at Go club…
-Hah.

09:29.652 --> 09:32.905
…but I'm lucky if I win one
out of ten matches with him.

09:32.989 --> 09:36.576
Everyone around him keeps filling him
with hot air, saying he's a prodigy,

09:37.535 --> 09:41.581
absorbed in this silly game
of stones instead of family business.

09:41.664 --> 09:45.042
Go's stature
has rising recently

09:45.126 --> 09:47.169
thanks to Champion Cho right here.

09:47.253 --> 09:49.380
There are more international competitions,

09:49.463 --> 09:52.592
so, you can enhance Korea's prestige too.

09:54.510 --> 09:56.804
-That's right.
-Yes.

09:58.556 --> 09:59.640
That being said,

10:00.349 --> 10:01.642
Champion Cho,

10:01.726 --> 10:05.730
I was hoping that you could perhaps
take the boy on for a few months.

10:05.813 --> 10:07.857
I would compensate you handsomely,

10:07.940 --> 10:10.443
and sponsor you generously, of course.

10:11.402 --> 10:14.113
You really should use that money
to send him abroad

10:14.864 --> 10:16.490
for the family business.

10:16.574 --> 10:18.993
You can't improve at Go by studying hard.

10:20.953 --> 10:23.122
There's really no point
in me taking him on.

10:24.248 --> 10:25.082
Talent?

10:26.584 --> 10:27.501
Not a pinch.

10:28.169 --> 10:29.837
No matter how hard I look.

10:33.215 --> 10:34.133
Pro Cho!

10:34.842 --> 10:36.552
Champion Cho!

10:37.678 --> 10:39.096
Hey, Cho Hoon-hyun!

10:41.265 --> 10:43.017
I worked for months trying to get that.

10:43.601 --> 10:46.395
Listen, man. You know
how much money he'll be sponsoring for us?

10:46.479 --> 10:48.064
What are we now, beggars?

10:48.564 --> 10:51.442
Business meetings, sponsorships,
they're all fine,

10:51.525 --> 10:53.444
but Go is more important than money.

10:54.362 --> 10:55.655
He said it was silly!

10:56.822 --> 10:57.782
Where's your pride?

10:58.699 --> 10:59.867
Pride?

11:17.468 --> 11:18.636
Min-je.

11:19.178 --> 11:21.389
Cho Min-je, what are you up to?

11:21.472 --> 11:22.765
-Daddy!
-Cho Min-je!

11:22.848 --> 11:24.600
Yah! Whoo-hoo!

11:24.684 --> 11:25.768
Ah, you're here!

11:25.851 --> 11:28.020
I made this for you, Daddy!

11:28.104 --> 11:31.315
Hey, Cho Min-je, I told you
not to touch the mail.

11:31.399 --> 11:32.775
Leave it, leave it.

11:32.858 --> 11:34.193
-I'll clean up.
-Come here.

11:34.276 --> 11:35.820
Is the mail interesting? Huh?

11:35.903 --> 11:38.739
Come on, let's go wash
your hands. Let's eat.

11:38.823 --> 11:42.034
Could you please turn on the stove?

11:42.118 --> 11:43.119
Let's go up.

11:43.202 --> 11:45.246
I want to eat sausage.

11:45.329 --> 11:47.331
You already had some this morning.

11:51.293 --> 11:53.254
KEEP YOUR PROMISE
FROM LEE CHANG-HO

11:58.050 --> 12:00.052
Aw, man.

12:01.137 --> 12:02.012
Hello?

12:02.096 --> 12:04.056
Hey, Pro Lee. Cho Hoon-hyun.

12:04.140 --> 12:05.725
Huh? Oh, right, yes.

12:06.308 --> 12:07.476
That boy, Chang-ho?

12:08.102 --> 12:09.645
Could I meet the boy again?

12:10.563 --> 12:11.439
LEE'S CLOCK SHOP

12:11.522 --> 12:14.024
-Oh, come on, let's go. Let's go.
-Hurry.

12:14.108 --> 12:16.944
SORRY, WE'RE CLOSED TODAY

12:20.364 --> 12:21.949
Only three handicap stones.

12:22.616 --> 12:25.077
But if I win, you'll teach me Go.

12:26.912 --> 12:28.205
Why learn Go from me?

12:28.289 --> 12:30.374
I heard you're the strongest player.

12:31.041 --> 12:32.460
Korea's best player.

12:32.543 --> 12:33.627
Hey, hey!

12:34.128 --> 12:38.132
Korea's best? He's the world's best.
You've got no idea kid.

12:38.758 --> 12:40.593
Hey. The masters are talking.

12:40.676 --> 12:43.220
Stop interrupting us, novice.

12:43.304 --> 12:45.765
You know, you're pretty rude
for a little kid.

12:45.848 --> 12:48.976
Last time, you little punk,
I gave four handicap stones.

12:49.059 --> 12:51.604
I'll knock you out
if we play an even game, you little brat!

12:51.687 --> 12:54.565
So you want to win
against a kid that badly, huh?

12:58.402 --> 12:59.403
And what about…

13:00.863 --> 13:02.406
if you lose, what's my prize?

13:07.369 --> 13:08.287
BANANA MILK

13:10.831 --> 13:12.792
Okay.

13:13.334 --> 13:17.421
It's a done deal.
Cho Hoon-hyun came all the way here.

13:18.130 --> 13:19.715
What a smart son you have.

13:19.799 --> 13:20.841
-Hwa-chun!
-Huh?

13:20.925 --> 13:22.468
Don't just stand there, come here.

13:22.551 --> 13:23.761
Ay!

13:23.844 --> 13:25.805
He's really nervous.

13:27.973 --> 13:29.850
Hmm.

13:47.117 --> 13:49.370
It looks like I can't make
anymore moves here.

13:49.453 --> 13:51.580
It's over. I won, right?

13:52.289 --> 13:55.376
Yeah, I lost this time. You've improved.

13:57.920 --> 14:01.382
Oh, you must be hungry.

14:01.465 --> 14:02.550
Right?

14:02.633 --> 14:04.802
Oh, but who won?

14:04.885 --> 14:06.387
Mr. Chang-ho just won.

14:06.470 --> 14:09.640
Oh wow, I can't believe it.

14:11.934 --> 14:14.270
Mr. Chang-ho, you're going to play again?

14:14.353 --> 14:17.523
It's one against one.
We're tied right now.

14:18.274 --> 14:19.984
So, do you like Go that much?

14:20.568 --> 14:23.863
It's awful.
When I lose, I can't sleep, I can't eat.

14:24.488 --> 14:26.323
It annoys me so much.

14:26.407 --> 14:29.326
But when I win,
there's nothing more fun in the world.

14:30.536 --> 14:32.246
Is that what keeps you playing, mister?

14:32.329 --> 14:34.665
Oh, he's not a kid.

14:36.792 --> 14:39.086
Let's, um…

14:40.462 --> 14:41.672
…finish up in Seoul.

14:44.717 --> 14:46.302
Oh my.

14:48.470 --> 14:50.890
Calling me "mister…" Amateur.

14:50.973 --> 14:53.309
Oh, I don't mean you.

14:55.561 --> 14:57.104
Call me "seonsaengnim."

14:57.187 --> 14:59.857
Seonsaengnim?

14:59.940 --> 15:01.066
-Goodness.
-Mm-hmm?

15:01.150 --> 15:03.360
He's in. He is in!

15:03.444 --> 15:05.112
Chang-ho, what are you doing?

15:05.195 --> 15:08.073
Bow to your seonsaengnim.
To your new teacher.

15:08.157 --> 15:11.160
-Oh no, that's all right.
-What are you doing keeping him?

15:11.243 --> 15:13.621
-Let's say hurray.
-Hurray!

15:13.704 --> 15:15.205
-Hurray for independence!
-Hurray!

15:18.083 --> 15:21.045
You play three-day matches.
How are you gonna handle a student?

15:21.545 --> 15:23.756
You really think you can handle all that?

15:23.839 --> 15:26.216
This is just between us,

15:26.300 --> 15:30.471
but you don't have the personality
to be a teacher, do you?

15:38.270 --> 15:40.397
Don't make more work for yourself, okay?

15:40.481 --> 15:41.690
Just focus on the match.

15:42.358 --> 15:45.235
What if you take him on as a student,
and he doesn't make it?

15:45.319 --> 15:47.571
So many people
already want to take you down.

15:47.655 --> 15:49.782
They'll go around saying
all sorts of crap.

15:49.907 --> 15:51.700
Wouldn't take him on
if going pro was the goal.

15:55.537 --> 15:58.916
I just got curious about
how he'd play when he's older.

16:00.501 --> 16:03.337
Chang-ho,
wear this at all times

16:03.420 --> 16:05.798
and think of this watch as me.

16:06.423 --> 16:07.800
Since you're doing this,

16:08.509 --> 16:10.552
give it your all so you won't regret it.

16:11.053 --> 16:14.014
Make sure to be studious and work hard.

16:14.890 --> 16:17.267
Make sure you listen to your seonsaengnim.

16:18.310 --> 16:19.395
Understand?

16:20.854 --> 16:21.897
Hmm.

16:47.840 --> 16:50.217
Champion Cho! Champion Cho!

16:50.300 --> 16:52.011
-Hey!
-You'll break the door.

16:52.094 --> 16:54.179
Hurry up! Hurry.

16:54.263 --> 16:56.807
Oh, gotta go! I gotta--

16:56.890 --> 16:58.267
What's with him?

17:00.811 --> 17:02.438
Right. Welcome.

17:02.521 --> 17:04.440
You must be tired. Come in.

17:13.866 --> 17:16.618
Oh,
I almost didn't make it.

17:17.870 --> 17:21.415
Oh my gosh! Sure are a handsome boy.

17:21.498 --> 17:24.585
Wow, look at those strong bones
and wide shoulders.

17:25.127 --> 17:26.378
Your wish has come true.

17:26.462 --> 17:28.714
Perfect build
for wrestling, yeah!

17:30.049 --> 17:32.468
-She's a girl.
-"She's a girl."

17:33.052 --> 17:35.971
Oh, ma'am, I didn't mean, uh…
Congratulations to you both!

17:36.055 --> 17:38.474
You've got two babies now!

17:38.557 --> 17:40.350
You're right about that.

17:40.434 --> 17:42.311
-You're Chang-ho, right?
-Yeah.

17:42.895 --> 17:43.729
How do you do?

17:48.776 --> 17:50.360
This is the study.

17:51.737 --> 17:54.031
If you wanna read anything, go ahead.

18:06.877 --> 18:08.378
I was about your age.

18:09.254 --> 18:10.756
Who's this older man?

18:12.007 --> 18:13.425
That's my seonsaengnim.

18:14.593 --> 18:15.677
Whoa.

18:16.220 --> 18:17.805
He looks so scary.

18:18.639 --> 18:22.142
-How old is he right now?
-He passed away a while ago.

18:23.811 --> 18:25.437
You're pretty lucky, huh?

18:26.105 --> 18:27.731
I'm not an old man quite yet.

18:29.525 --> 18:33.112
My grandpa said
that death doesn't care about your age.

18:36.824 --> 18:37.825
Let's go eat.

18:39.409 --> 18:40.285
Come on.

18:43.413 --> 18:46.917
This liquor is Igangju,
but I don't feel drunk.

18:47.000 --> 18:49.044
-It deserves it's liquor of Joseon title.
-Yeah.

18:49.128 --> 18:52.965
Tell your grandpa
I appreciate it very much, okay?

18:53.048 --> 18:54.508
-Yes.
-How is the food?

18:54.591 --> 18:55.968
Does everything taste okay?

18:56.051 --> 18:57.511
Yes. It's delicious.

18:57.594 --> 18:59.555
You're a wonderful cook, madam.

19:00.055 --> 19:03.517
"Madam," um…
That doesn't sound right.

19:04.935 --> 19:06.937
Yeah. We're family now.

19:07.729 --> 19:08.605
That's a weird name.

19:09.398 --> 19:11.024
I have to call her something.

19:11.733 --> 19:14.570
-I'm not sure what to call her.
-He's right about that.

19:14.653 --> 19:16.238
Titles, once they get mixed up…

19:17.990 --> 19:18.824
are confusing.

19:22.327 --> 19:23.453
What about "Auntie"?

19:24.246 --> 19:26.707
Just call me "Auntie"
from now on. That's nice.

19:29.251 --> 19:30.085
Okay.

19:32.171 --> 19:33.505
Want some more rice, Chang-ho?

19:34.298 --> 19:37.426
Yes. A little more please. Thanks, Auntie.

19:39.303 --> 19:40.679
FUMIGATION

19:55.736 --> 19:57.404
KOREA BADUK ASSOCIATION

19:57.487 --> 20:01.283
CONGRATULATIONS
CHO HOON-HYUN CONQUERS THE WORLD

20:08.290 --> 20:09.374
Who are you?

20:09.458 --> 20:10.792
Looking for your dad?

20:10.876 --> 20:12.336
No, it's not that.

20:13.003 --> 20:15.339
I'm here to play some Go.

20:15.422 --> 20:16.590
Play Go?

20:27.476 --> 20:28.435
Who's that?

20:29.019 --> 20:31.104
I heard
he's Champion Cho's student.

20:31.605 --> 20:33.023
Anyone else?

20:35.317 --> 20:36.485
Where'd he come from?

20:36.568 --> 20:38.654
Wow, he's amazing, seriously.

20:38.737 --> 20:39.905
He's like a pro.

20:40.530 --> 20:42.783
Whoa, he's pushing it like that?

20:43.533 --> 20:44.993
I've never seen that before.

20:48.956 --> 20:50.540
Whoa, what was that?

20:50.624 --> 20:52.668
Agh! Come on, really?

20:53.627 --> 20:56.588
There's so many.
I'll play everyone at once.

20:56.672 --> 20:58.715
This kid is crazy.

21:11.770 --> 21:14.314
Wow, he really must be a prodigy.

21:15.107 --> 21:18.235
Champion Cho wouldn't have brought
him in from Jeonju if he wasn't.

21:18.318 --> 21:21.405
Yeah, Champion Cho found
a really good one.

21:23.156 --> 21:24.908
-He's really good.
-He is.

21:34.960 --> 21:37.004
Ah!

21:40.090 --> 21:42.134
There's a territory
here and here.

21:42.217 --> 21:44.553
And if you add the komi,
it's at least twenty.

21:45.512 --> 21:46.638
Want more?

21:50.350 --> 21:52.311
HOSTED BY KOREA BADUK ASSOCIATION
SEJONG HOTEL

21:52.394 --> 21:54.521
NINTH GUKGI CHALLENGE MATCH
FOURTH ROUND

21:54.604 --> 21:56.898
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS NAM GI-CHEOL 8-DAN

21:59.443 --> 22:01.695
Mr. 9-dan Cho, 30 minutes left.

22:01.778 --> 22:03.697
CHALLENGE MATCH: FINAL MATCH

22:03.780 --> 22:06.074
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN, NAM GI-CHEOL 8-DAN

22:07.701 --> 22:10.704
Champion Cho has a core of steel.
He's brutal.

22:10.787 --> 22:13.623
He won the match 30 minutes ago.
Why is he waiting?

22:13.707 --> 22:16.877
Expert Nam gets my respect
because, I mean,

22:16.960 --> 22:18.462
this has happened before,

22:18.545 --> 22:21.173
and he knows it'll get ugly
if he keeps going.

22:21.256 --> 22:23.300
Ah, I'm sick of this era of Cho and Nam.

22:24.009 --> 22:26.845
Nam Gi-cheol 8-dan,
this is your final byoyomi.

22:27.554 --> 22:33.060
And one, two, three, four…

22:33.143 --> 22:34.186
Five.

22:35.103 --> 22:36.104
…six,

22:36.688 --> 22:38.690
seven, eight…

22:38.774 --> 22:40.359
…nine.

22:47.240 --> 22:48.784
I mean…

22:50.327 --> 22:52.079
…should have blocked it there.

22:54.998 --> 22:56.124
What a wuss.

23:13.558 --> 23:15.811
He's doing it. The Rattler.

23:15.894 --> 23:17.437
What's the Rattler?

23:17.521 --> 23:19.648
Hey, you don't know that? Huh?

23:19.731 --> 23:23.110
If Cho Hoon-hyun starts bouncing his leg,
that match is a sure win.

23:23.693 --> 23:27.072
It's like Seon Dong-yeol stretching
in the bullpen in a game of baseball.

23:27.155 --> 23:28.073
Oh.

23:28.156 --> 23:30.367
It makes the opponent
lose their concentration.

23:33.829 --> 23:34.663
One,

23:35.372 --> 23:36.206
two,

23:36.957 --> 23:37.791
three,

23:38.375 --> 23:39.251
four…

23:39.334 --> 23:43.004
♪ The drizzle makes no sound ♪

23:43.630 --> 23:47.801
♪ We part at Busan station in sorrow ♪

23:49.469 --> 23:54.683
♪ Goodbye, farewell ♪

23:54.766 --> 23:57.436
♪ The train whistles as tears fall ♪

24:02.357 --> 24:04.568
A no-count win
by Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan.

24:04.651 --> 24:07.237
NO-COUNT WIN: A WIN SO DECISIVE
YOU WIN WITHOUT COUNTING TERRITORIES

24:07.946 --> 24:10.407
Expert Nam seemed really angry today.

24:10.490 --> 24:14.411
Still, he should put back the stones.
Wow, what bad manners! Hmm.

24:14.494 --> 24:17.372
You, giving a lecture on manners?
"Parting at Busan"?

24:18.248 --> 24:21.543
You need to grind them into the ground,
to make it easier the next time.

24:21.626 --> 24:24.129
Don't worry. He'll be back
for revenge later. You'll see.

24:24.963 --> 24:29.176
Aigo! Congratulations!
Your song selection was great today.

24:29.259 --> 24:32.304
I already see the headlines
that'll be up tomorrow.

24:32.387 --> 24:36.141
Ah, Mr. Chang-ho is going through
Gwancheol-dong as we speak.

24:36.224 --> 24:39.394
He's mowing through all the apprentices
like they're grass.

24:39.478 --> 24:41.396
Word has spread everywhere

24:41.480 --> 24:44.024
that the tiger cub you brought back
is a total prodigy.

24:44.107 --> 24:45.484
Yeah, but…

24:45.567 --> 24:48.945
Hey, don't mention that prodigy stuff
around him. Just don't do it.

24:49.821 --> 24:51.072
It won't do him any good.

24:54.201 --> 24:55.327
Wait for me.

24:56.620 --> 24:57.829
Seonsaengnim.

24:59.247 --> 25:01.791
-What's this?
-Candy.

25:02.876 --> 25:03.960
We're here, Auntie.

25:04.044 --> 25:05.212
Oh. You're together?

25:06.338 --> 25:07.756
We ran into each other.

25:07.839 --> 25:10.342
-You did well, Chang-ho?
-Yes. Thanks, Auntie.

25:10.425 --> 25:11.635
How was the match today?

25:12.761 --> 25:13.845
-I lost.
-Hmm.

25:14.888 --> 25:16.431
You always say you lost.

25:21.144 --> 25:24.564
The opening, haengma, reading,
they're all terrible.

25:24.648 --> 25:26.233
TO THINK IN ADVANCE
WHERE TO PLACE A STONE

25:26.316 --> 25:28.151
But do you know what's worst among those?

25:28.235 --> 25:29.986
It is your terrible attitude.

25:30.070 --> 25:31.071
Huh?

25:31.905 --> 25:33.615
I won against everyone.

25:33.698 --> 25:36.284
The older players
weren't anything special.

25:36.368 --> 25:37.869
Winning isn't everything.

25:38.870 --> 25:43.500
You've only studied Go a few months.
These guys have been studying for years.

25:44.167 --> 25:46.503
Your moves got lazy
since you were at an advantage.

25:46.586 --> 25:51.132
It's good manners to always do your best.
And learn to respect your opponent first.

25:51.216 --> 25:52.968
But you shake your leg.

25:53.677 --> 25:55.679
You do. And you hum.

25:55.762 --> 25:56.596
You…

25:57.722 --> 25:59.140
Hey…

26:01.434 --> 26:02.477
Hey, punk…

26:04.813 --> 26:06.898
save that for when you're the best.

26:09.859 --> 26:10.986
Let's, uh…

26:13.613 --> 26:15.407
We'll start with the basics.

26:16.157 --> 26:17.450
But I read that book.

26:17.993 --> 26:20.579
Basics are boring, and they're easy.

26:20.662 --> 26:21.705
Easy?

26:24.416 --> 26:28.169
-Black or white, what's better?
-White has the advantage. It's obvious.

26:33.758 --> 26:34.634
Take white.

26:42.434 --> 26:45.145
Good moves don't come
from thinking for a long time.

26:45.228 --> 26:46.813
Thinking is what bad players do.

26:47.606 --> 26:49.524
It's time to cultivate game sense.

26:50.525 --> 26:52.277
That doesn't mean play impulsively.

26:54.487 --> 26:55.822
Don't back down.

26:56.406 --> 26:58.575
The essence of Go is
the battle, the attack.

27:01.870 --> 27:03.288
Still think white's better?

27:05.415 --> 27:06.416
I don't.

27:07.417 --> 27:08.376
Take black.

27:23.141 --> 27:26.353
I played only using the basics.
Tell me why you're losing.

27:30.857 --> 27:33.818
"Genius," "prodigy," don't believe
when people mention that.

27:34.361 --> 27:36.529
You're good at calculations
and memorizing.

27:37.030 --> 27:38.948
You're only imitating how to play Go.

27:40.825 --> 27:42.619
Don't be cocky. Learn the basics.

27:46.915 --> 27:49.709
Use your right hand when playing,
if nothing else.

27:49.793 --> 27:52.253
It is basic courtesy
when playing your opponent.

27:53.630 --> 27:54.464
Okay.

27:56.800 --> 27:58.343
Stamina is everything.

27:59.260 --> 28:01.304
The rashness of an impulsive move.

28:02.138 --> 28:04.766
The complacency of wanting to compromise.

28:05.558 --> 28:07.686
The arrogance of wanting
to finish quickly.

28:08.228 --> 28:10.855
These things happen
when your stamina fails,

28:10.939 --> 28:13.108
and they'll lead to your defeat.

28:25.036 --> 28:27.497
Ah, no. I'll use my right hand.

28:39.259 --> 28:41.469
DEAR GRANDPA
I HOPE YOU'RE WELL

29:33.396 --> 29:35.774
ONE STEP, ONE MOVE

29:35.857 --> 29:37.066
Ugh…

29:39.319 --> 29:42.697
Who eats Chinese food on the rooftop?
Are you kidding me?

30:21.820 --> 30:22.654
Hello.

30:22.737 --> 30:24.197
Do you always come up here?

30:27.200 --> 30:29.327
Man! Couldn't they have ordered together?

30:30.286 --> 30:33.122
What's their problem?
Why can't they eat at the restaurant?

30:36.334 --> 30:39.212
Champion Cho must be working like crazy
to keep you fed.

30:41.673 --> 30:42.549
Do you…

30:44.300 --> 30:45.677
know who I am?

30:46.261 --> 30:48.012
Yeah, of course I know who you are.

30:49.097 --> 30:52.183
You're the pro Nam Gi-cheol,
my seonsaengnim's rival.

30:53.268 --> 30:54.310
Rival? Please.

30:55.728 --> 30:57.188
"KING OF GO" EXPANDS HIS FOOTPRINT

30:57.272 --> 30:59.691
Don't relax now that you're a pro.
Keep studying.

30:59.774 --> 31:01.568
Your teacher is extremely good.

31:01.651 --> 31:02.610
Well,

31:04.279 --> 31:05.154
you see,

31:07.240 --> 31:10.201
I'm not sure if it's something
I can learn just by studying.

31:11.870 --> 31:14.581
I would love to be just half
as good as his pinky toe,

31:16.374 --> 31:18.459
but I just don't seem to have the talent.

31:20.879 --> 31:23.006
Don't just try to learn.

31:23.631 --> 31:24.841
You should try to win.

31:26.718 --> 31:28.678
Then you'll naturally learn.

31:29.512 --> 31:31.347
That's what I did when I played him.

31:36.853 --> 31:40.231
CHO HOON-HYUN'S LEGENDARY MATCHES

31:40.315 --> 31:42.150
WHITE CHO HOON-HYUN
BLACK KIM SEONG-JU

31:49.908 --> 31:51.910
Wow, it moves so quickly.

31:52.869 --> 31:54.579
How do I capture this?

31:55.538 --> 31:57.790
Maybe going head-on won't help at all.

31:58.875 --> 32:00.585
Should I just hold?

32:19.228 --> 32:22.190
Chang-ho is working late tonight.

32:22.732 --> 32:23.733
Mm-hmm.

32:24.692 --> 32:26.319
So, how's it going?

32:27.487 --> 32:29.238
Preliminaries are coming up, right?

32:29.864 --> 32:32.158
How he does right now isn't important.

32:33.409 --> 32:35.036
It's about finding his own Go.

32:36.412 --> 32:38.623
You know, rushing him
won't do him any good.

32:39.248 --> 32:42.168
Don't just push him,
coax and soothe him, honey.

32:42.251 --> 32:43.252
Chang-ho's still a kid.

32:43.878 --> 32:46.130
He'll be spoiled if I baby him like a kid.

32:47.882 --> 32:49.175
I made him come to Seoul.

32:50.051 --> 32:53.179
I can't slack off in teaching him.
I need to make him the best.

32:54.389 --> 32:57.392
Competition life is too sad if

32:58.810 --> 33:00.228
you're not top dog.

33:01.396 --> 33:04.357
SEVENTH DAEWANG TOURNAMENT
FIRST PRELIMINARY ROUND

33:40.393 --> 33:44.647
I mean, he keeps staring at the board
like it'll magically move or something.

33:45.148 --> 33:48.192
You know, I thought
he was falling asleep during the match.

33:49.610 --> 33:52.613
You know, the kid plays Go
like he's pushing 60 years old.

33:53.573 --> 33:55.992
-He's lost two rounds in a row.
-Aish!

33:56.075 --> 33:59.162
-Hey, Pro Noh, how much did you lose?
-A couple hundred.

33:59.245 --> 34:00.079
Hmm.

34:00.163 --> 34:02.248
I'm losing all my earnings
on bets like this.

34:03.207 --> 34:06.044
I heard he was Cho's student,
so I thought he'd be winning more.

34:06.127 --> 34:10.006
I mean, he used to be a bright kid,
so why's he been getting worse?

34:10.089 --> 34:12.300
And his personality
is getting weirder too.

34:12.383 --> 34:16.095
Champion Cho probably hounds him
all day and night with that temper of his.

34:16.179 --> 34:19.474
And he's living with him too,
so it makes sense.

34:22.685 --> 34:23.644
Grandpa…

34:24.520 --> 34:27.482
Seonsaengnim Cho's Go
is flashy and strong,

34:27.565 --> 34:29.025
but it doesn't suit me.

34:29.525 --> 34:31.402
I'm going to find my own Go,

34:32.028 --> 34:36.491
something no one else can replicate,
even if it takes time.

34:38.367 --> 34:40.036
That's not it!

34:40.119 --> 34:43.331
The geima at the top right corner,
attach, push at the top edge, extending.

34:43.414 --> 34:44.874
Where is everything I've taught you?

34:44.957 --> 34:46.042
Honey.

34:46.834 --> 34:48.503
-It's getting late.
-Leave us.

34:48.586 --> 34:50.296
You can't win all the time.

34:50.379 --> 34:52.924
He's already upset
about the loss, you know.

34:53.007 --> 34:54.592
Stay out of it, please.

34:59.639 --> 35:02.850
You hold when you should push
and push when you should hold.

35:03.518 --> 35:04.602
Why are you offbeat?

35:06.395 --> 35:09.565
I thought the variables
would increase with a fight,

35:09.649 --> 35:11.400
so it'd be better to wait until--

35:11.484 --> 35:12.527
I told you.

35:13.444 --> 35:16.322
Go isn't about compromising
and building territories.

35:16.906 --> 35:18.825
Instead, you need to bite,
scratch, and claw!

35:20.910 --> 35:23.412
That's not my style, seonsaengnim.
That is what you'd do.

35:23.496 --> 35:24.622
Don't give me lip--

35:24.705 --> 35:25.790
Style?

35:26.707 --> 35:27.750
Play style?

35:28.334 --> 35:30.169
Lose and none of that stuff matters!

35:30.670 --> 35:32.797
Learn to play! Follow the pattern.

35:33.464 --> 35:36.968
Does everyone in the world need
to play Go the same as you?

35:37.051 --> 35:39.137
All I'm saying is there's an order!

35:40.096 --> 35:43.307
You need to have a reason
for every stone you put down.

35:43.391 --> 35:45.268
A reason behind every retreat.

35:46.102 --> 35:50.022
You can't make your own style
or anything without the basics!

35:55.903 --> 35:57.780
It's the same here.

35:58.781 --> 36:03.077
It's only natural to extend over here,
so why would you retreat? Why?

36:04.287 --> 36:05.496
Why are you so defiant?

36:08.708 --> 36:12.336
I know that might be what's right,
but there is a…

36:13.671 --> 36:15.464
small chance tables turn.

36:16.132 --> 36:19.510
And if I make this move,

36:19.594 --> 36:21.095
I'm one hundred percent sure

36:22.930 --> 36:24.640
that I'll keep half a point.

36:25.474 --> 36:26.475
A hundred percent?

36:27.268 --> 36:29.687
Chang-ho, how many times did I tell you

36:30.438 --> 36:33.691
staking out territories in the center
becomes too much of a risk!

36:33.774 --> 36:35.902
I'm sure that you're right, but…

36:38.362 --> 36:41.032
…I thought I could do
the calculations, so…

36:42.867 --> 36:44.577
…uh, I experimented here.

36:46.662 --> 36:47.830
Experimented?

36:50.750 --> 36:52.418
You think Go is a piece of cake.

36:53.794 --> 36:57.089
You disregard the basics,
use petty tricks instead,

36:57.173 --> 36:59.300
and stubbornly cling to your own ideas.

37:03.387 --> 37:04.222
Let's stop.

37:05.431 --> 37:08.601
There's no point in getting angry
when you don't want to learn.

37:22.198 --> 37:25.284
And if I make this move,

37:25.368 --> 37:27.119
I'm one hundred percent sure

37:28.871 --> 37:30.706
that I'll keep half a point.

37:34.126 --> 37:37.046
Those who play first,
have the advantage in Go.

37:37.630 --> 37:39.548
When players of the same rank play,

37:40.091 --> 37:43.052
the first player is disadvantaged
five and a half points.

37:44.220 --> 37:45.429
That's called komi.

37:48.766 --> 37:51.519
The half a point here is to prevent a tie,

37:52.228 --> 37:54.647
and such a thing
does not actually exist on the board.

37:58.025 --> 38:00.820
It's the minimum unit deciding a match

38:00.903 --> 38:03.239
and does not visibly exist on the board.

38:04.782 --> 38:06.701
Perhaps, this kid
is seeing something else here.

38:06.784 --> 38:08.995
BLACK WINS BY 1.5 POINTS

38:23.092 --> 38:25.011
RESPECTFULLY YOURS, CHANG-HO

38:30.016 --> 38:33.019
SIR, AUNTIE, THANK YOU FOR EVERYTHING
SORRY TO DISAPPOINT YOU

38:40.192 --> 38:41.068
Yes, where to?

38:42.486 --> 38:44.405
9:40 bus to Jeonju, please.

38:44.488 --> 38:46.115
All right, 9:40 bus to Jeonju!

38:46.198 --> 38:47.408
SEOUL - JEONJU

38:47.491 --> 38:49.410
The 9:40 bus is now leaving!

38:50.411 --> 38:52.747
Okay, okay, anyone else boarding?

38:53.831 --> 38:55.791
Okay, we have everyone, right?

39:06.427 --> 39:07.678
Aigo!

39:08.387 --> 39:10.306
Seonsaengnim.

39:26.072 --> 39:27.031
Yesterday,

39:28.783 --> 39:31.911
the half point you talked about,

39:33.287 --> 39:36.290
it turns out you weren't completely wrong.

39:36.832 --> 39:38.667
It doesn't make it right, though.

39:39.168 --> 39:40.044
I just

39:41.587 --> 39:43.214
haven't found the right move yet.

39:50.096 --> 39:51.889
Go doesn't have answers,

39:53.849 --> 39:55.768
but I was forcing you to give me one.

39:58.020 --> 39:58.896
I'm sorry.

40:00.189 --> 40:01.524
Better to walk steady

40:02.400 --> 40:04.110
than try to run and wobble.

40:05.903 --> 40:07.988
You found your Go. That's good enough.

40:11.492 --> 40:13.285
If that's the decision you've made,

40:13.786 --> 40:15.079
take responsibility.

40:16.038 --> 40:17.039
In both Go

40:18.040 --> 40:18.916
and in life.

40:22.586 --> 40:23.629
Understand?

40:32.888 --> 40:35.099
Your fighting spirit is eighty percent.

40:36.350 --> 40:38.811
Even if you lose,
you can't let them take you in spirit.

40:39.770 --> 40:40.938
It's better to hide it.

40:41.480 --> 40:45.109
Your thoughts, emotions, your breathing.

40:46.318 --> 40:48.487
Do not show vulnerability
to your opponent.

40:49.363 --> 40:52.658
I know, but, um, it's not easy to do.

40:52.741 --> 40:56.162
Think about something
familiar and comfortable.

40:57.580 --> 41:00.583
Something that just relaxes you
by thinking of it.

41:02.209 --> 41:05.004
The match is over
the moment you lose your composure.

41:10.926 --> 41:13.095
Don't view the stones by color.

41:14.889 --> 41:16.932
Every move needs a reason behind it.

41:17.600 --> 41:18.809
Territories

41:19.977 --> 41:23.439
come into form naturally
and cannot be built with force.

41:24.482 --> 41:26.484
Take care of each and every stone.

41:27.735 --> 41:28.694
At some point,

41:29.487 --> 41:32.239
the stones will have moved
towards harmony.

41:35.034 --> 41:39.830
29TH CHOEGOWI FINAL PRELIMINARY

41:43.667 --> 41:45.211
Aren't you going up?

41:45.294 --> 41:46.378
Don't have to.

41:47.046 --> 41:51.717
Aigo. Mr. Chang-ho just had to end up
with Pro Ko again, the old-timer.

41:51.800 --> 41:54.386
Hey, don't worry about him.

41:54.470 --> 41:57.765
You should be
figuring out how to survive Chang-ho.

41:58.349 --> 41:59.558
He's an odd one.

42:00.059 --> 42:03.312
Doesn't even review his games properly,
but he somehow keeps getting better.

42:03.395 --> 42:05.481
REVIEW: TO REPLAY A FINISHED GAME
AND GO OVER THE MOVES

42:06.565 --> 42:10.027
His opening is sloppy
and his haengma is slow,

42:10.778 --> 42:12.696
but he somehow builds a position.

42:13.322 --> 42:16.659
His calculations
might be better than mine.

42:17.159 --> 42:20.162
So does he still play
like he's a 60-year-old grandfather?

42:20.246 --> 42:21.247
No.

42:22.248 --> 42:23.249
Like he's 80.

42:32.675 --> 42:35.386
I'm going to protect
half a point for certainty

42:35.469 --> 42:38.138
rather than make a whole point
through a fight.

42:38.931 --> 42:42.393
In the end, Go is a fight for territories.

42:44.228 --> 42:48.065
Grandpa, I think
I've finally found my own Go.

42:48.732 --> 42:50.234
It's a bit rough,

42:50.317 --> 42:53.112
and it's not flashy
like Seonsaengnim Cho's,

42:53.862 --> 42:58.158
but it's going to be impossible
for anyone to beat.

43:03.455 --> 43:05.624
-That's good.
-Yeah, that's a good piece.

43:10.045 --> 43:13.424
The energy must be excellent
here at Yeonhui-dong, right?

43:14.008 --> 43:16.677
Two soaring professional players
under the same roof.

43:18.095 --> 43:20.264
Chang-ho, sir, congratulations!

43:20.347 --> 43:23.267
You're making good time,
already heading to finals!

43:23.350 --> 43:26.687
Shouldn't we take a photograph
to remember this?

43:27.771 --> 43:30.816
Pro Cheon, could you take
a family photo for us?

43:30.899 --> 43:32.776
Yeah.

43:39.617 --> 43:40.618
Now…

43:40.701 --> 43:42.119
One, two!

43:43.621 --> 43:45.080
Chang-ho, come on, kid, smile.

43:45.164 --> 43:46.415
Why do you look so sad?

43:47.333 --> 43:49.084
What? He's smiling really big.

43:49.710 --> 43:50.794
Yeah, he's smiling.

43:51.712 --> 43:53.172
-Oh, really?
-Yes.

43:54.214 --> 43:56.216
O-Okay, then, here we go. Ready?

43:56.842 --> 43:59.803
One, two, three!

44:04.767 --> 44:05.976
But I think

44:06.852 --> 44:09.438
it'd be better for the white
to bend this way here.

44:10.064 --> 44:12.066
That could be a good move, but…

44:13.275 --> 44:15.319
I'm thinking it could leave an opening.

44:15.402 --> 44:17.321
Still, it'd be simple to cut off.

44:20.949 --> 44:22.451
You're not even leaping there,

44:22.534 --> 44:24.495
you'd rather take the long way around.

44:25.954 --> 44:27.289
I don't love it, but…

44:27.373 --> 44:31.543
…well, no one
will be judging me for it, either.

44:33.379 --> 44:34.380
Who are you playing?

44:35.255 --> 44:36.757
I'm playing Pro Nam Gi-cheol.

44:38.842 --> 44:41.387
I'm, uh… I'm worried about it.

44:41.470 --> 44:44.139
I mean, his Go is fierce,
but you know this, of course.

44:44.765 --> 44:46.058
He's persistent.

44:47.434 --> 44:50.938
If you start to back down, he'll think
you're weak and start attacking.

44:51.563 --> 44:53.148
You need to come at him strong.

44:53.899 --> 44:55.651
I'm going to start in defense mode.

44:55.734 --> 44:57.152
You little punk!

44:59.029 --> 45:01.156
You told me I should find my own Go.

45:01.240 --> 45:02.574
Should I stand back?

45:04.368 --> 45:05.619
Believe in me.

45:06.870 --> 45:07.788
Okay.

45:08.831 --> 45:10.791
Think of it as a lesson. Don't be nervous.

45:11.959 --> 45:12.793
Okay.

45:15.546 --> 45:16.505
I'm going…

45:17.631 --> 45:19.091
I'm going to beat him.

45:21.218 --> 45:26.724
23RD WANGWI COMPETITION FINALS 12TH ROUND

45:40.112 --> 45:41.488
Nam 9-dan, black.

45:42.072 --> 45:43.574
Lee 3-dan, white.

45:45.617 --> 45:46.785
Let the match begin.

45:46.869 --> 45:49.121
29TH CHOEGOWI MATCH
CHALLENGER SELECTION

45:49.204 --> 45:51.498
NAM GI-CHEOL 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 3-DAN

46:04.803 --> 46:05.721
Mr. Lee.

46:05.804 --> 46:07.139
Oh! My goodness.

46:07.222 --> 46:09.516
Why don't we go to the review room,
have some fresh coffee?

46:09.600 --> 46:12.519
Ah, no. I won't understand
anything anyway.

46:12.603 --> 46:14.021
-It's all right.
-Ah.

46:55.896 --> 46:58.774
Cho 9-dan, ten minutes left.

46:59.775 --> 47:01.109
Oh, uh… uh…

47:01.693 --> 47:02.820
Okay…

47:10.202 --> 47:12.162
I… Well, uh…

47:12.704 --> 47:15.916
No-count win for white,
Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan.

47:18.919 --> 47:20.087
Oh, Pro Baek.

47:21.129 --> 47:22.381
Thank you for the lesson.

47:25.217 --> 47:27.386
Hey, Champion Cho.

47:27.970 --> 47:29.847
The black seems to be at an advantage.

47:29.930 --> 47:32.057
Oh, and what would you know about that?

47:32.140 --> 47:33.684
Didn't you get crushed too?

47:33.767 --> 47:36.645
I didn't get crushed, you punk.
I was drunk that day.

47:36.728 --> 47:38.856
Here's the record to the 115th move.

47:40.440 --> 47:41.608
Mm-hmm.

47:56.248 --> 47:58.917
Shouldn't have cut that. Huh?

48:00.127 --> 48:01.920
If I took it…

48:06.592 --> 48:10.053
Push one
and expand to the center.

48:19.563 --> 48:22.149
A game between you and Champion Cho
will be worth watching.

48:23.066 --> 48:23.942
Hmm?

48:26.194 --> 48:28.447
You're better than your teacher
in closing.

48:29.489 --> 48:30.407
Congratulations.

48:37.331 --> 48:38.957
Expert Nam collapsed at the end.

48:39.041 --> 48:42.085
See, man? Chang-ho's just strong.
I'm not weak.

48:42.169 --> 48:44.212
Something about that energy
in Yeonhui-dong.

48:44.296 --> 48:45.380
29TH CHOEGOWI TOURNAMENT

48:47.716 --> 48:49.843
LEE CHANG-HO

48:49.927 --> 48:50.761
CHALLENGER

48:59.519 --> 49:01.146
Oh my.

49:01.855 --> 49:03.941
I cannot believe
that this match has come so quickly.

49:04.024 --> 49:06.026
CHOEGOWI FINAL
LEE CHANG-HO VS CHO HOON-HYUN

49:06.109 --> 49:08.028
He won his way up. What can I say?

49:09.696 --> 49:11.323
What happens if Chang-ho
actually beats ya?

49:11.406 --> 49:13.033
Oh yeah? Please.

49:13.575 --> 49:15.243
In ten years, maybe.

49:17.454 --> 49:20.457
Please watch your step
while exiting the train.

49:23.585 --> 49:24.419
Doors closing.

49:30.968 --> 49:33.345
WINS THE YING SHIBEI CUP!
UNIFIES THE WORLD!

50:07.504 --> 50:09.006
CHO HOON-HYUN
SEO GEON-WOO

50:14.886 --> 50:16.847
Seonsaengnim's haengma is weak

50:17.556 --> 50:19.307
when he's been attacked in a game.

50:22.310 --> 50:26.940
When the framework expands,
his check is always weak.

50:33.864 --> 50:35.407
Seonsaengnim, dinner's ready.

50:35.490 --> 50:36.491
Yeah.

50:39.911 --> 50:41.621
Ah, here's the book.

50:55.969 --> 50:59.765
Hey, uh, honey, come on,
you should talk to him.

50:59.848 --> 51:01.475
You're his seonsaengnim, right?

51:02.184 --> 51:03.351
What do you want me to…

51:04.186 --> 51:06.938
Did you sleep well? Are you okay?

51:07.564 --> 51:08.607
I'm good, Auntie.

51:10.358 --> 51:11.902
Don't get hung up on winning.

51:14.237 --> 51:15.781
Just play your own way.

51:18.658 --> 51:19.493
Yes.

51:21.369 --> 51:22.871
-Is that the car?
-Yes, it is.

51:22.954 --> 51:25.165
FEBRUARY 2ND 1990
KOREA BADUK ASSOCIATION, GWANCHEOL-DONG

51:25.248 --> 51:26.875
-They came in the same car.
-Get a photo!

51:26.958 --> 51:30.212
Champion Cho, will you open
aggressively today as well?

51:30.295 --> 51:32.214
Will you go easy on your student?

51:32.297 --> 51:34.633
Wait, wait.

51:39.304 --> 51:40.138
You'll do well.

51:41.014 --> 51:41.848
Thanks.

52:25.016 --> 52:26.643
Choose your stones, please.

52:41.449 --> 52:45.162
Lee 4-dan's black. Cho 9-dan's white.

52:47.914 --> 52:49.249
Let the game begin.

52:49.332 --> 52:51.042
29TH CHOEGOWI CHALLENGE MATCH
LAST ROUND

52:51.126 --> 52:54.588
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 4-DAN

52:56.464 --> 52:57.841
COUNTDOWN

53:44.888 --> 53:45.764
Hey, let's see.

53:45.847 --> 53:47.849
Pro Cheon,
how many moves have been made?

53:47.933 --> 53:49.935
Just a sec. Reporters, please!

53:50.018 --> 53:51.436
I haven't taken a look at it yet.

53:51.519 --> 53:53.104
Ack, later, please! People!

53:53.188 --> 53:54.522
Sure! Sure!

53:54.606 --> 53:57.025
Yeah, later, later. Okay. All right.

53:57.108 --> 53:58.151
Jeez.

53:58.235 --> 53:59.444
Ugh, it's so hectic.

54:01.238 --> 54:03.949
Whoa, it's a fierce opening
from Champion Cho.

54:04.032 --> 54:06.743
See? It's an onslaught from the beginning.

54:07.244 --> 54:11.706
Oh my. He's being so ruthless
against his young student. Right?

54:11.790 --> 54:14.167
-That's really brutal of him.
-Huh.

54:30.517 --> 54:32.060
TIME SPENT

54:32.143 --> 54:35.272
LEE CHANG-HO 2 HOURS 10 MINUTES
CHO HOON-HYUN 50 MINUTES

54:42.237 --> 54:44.531
This game will resume again after lunch.

54:48.451 --> 54:50.328
Should I have just taken it?

54:51.621 --> 54:54.374
A knight's jump,
then a two-space extension.

54:56.835 --> 54:59.129
Maybe
I should have given up a point.

55:05.427 --> 55:08.054
Great-grandpa,
when did you get here?

55:08.888 --> 55:10.348
Oh, this morning.

55:10.432 --> 55:11.891
Ah.

55:13.059 --> 55:16.771
Oh, but Chang-ho seems off his game today.

55:16.855 --> 55:19.774
Oh, he was ruthless playing
against me last time.

55:19.858 --> 55:21.359
What's this discrimination about?

55:22.652 --> 55:26.948
Oh, ask Seonsaengnim to go easy on you,
cut you some slack.

55:27.032 --> 55:29.743
What are you talking about?
A match is a match.

55:35.165 --> 55:36.624
He is such a…

55:39.210 --> 55:40.712
Oh, good, food's here.

55:43.965 --> 55:46.634
Oh, careful, this is hot. It's hot.

55:46.718 --> 55:47.677
Oh, oh, oh.

55:47.761 --> 55:50.597
-Hey, waitress!
-Some water, please.

57:05.004 --> 57:08.716
Huh, Mr. Chang-ho seems to be making
small mistakes today.

57:08.800 --> 57:12.512
We can't compete with him,
so how could a kid do that?

57:14.180 --> 57:15.974
It's his seonsaengnim. He looks up to him.

57:37.203 --> 57:38.788
TIME SPENT

57:38.872 --> 57:42.125
LEE CHANG-HO 3 HOURS 51 MINUTES
CHO HOON-HYUN 1 HOUR 43 MINUTES

57:50.550 --> 57:53.344
Think about something
familiar and comfortable.

57:53.428 --> 57:56.890
Something that just relaxes you
by thinking of it.

57:59.559 --> 58:02.228
The match is over
the moment you lose your composure.

01:00:21.075 --> 01:00:22.410
TIME SPENT

01:00:22.493 --> 01:00:26.331
LEE CHANG-HO 3 HOURS 53 MINUTES
CHO HOON-HYUN 2 HOUR 58 MINUTES

01:00:57.028 --> 01:00:57.987
Cho 9-dan.

01:00:58.780 --> 01:00:59.614
One,

01:01:00.448 --> 01:01:01.282
two,

01:01:02.033 --> 01:01:02.867
three,

01:01:03.409 --> 01:01:04.243
four,

01:01:05.036 --> 01:01:05.870
five,

01:01:06.704 --> 01:01:07.538
six,

01:01:08.456 --> 01:01:09.791
seven…

01:01:09.874 --> 01:01:10.792
…eight,

01:01:11.501 --> 01:01:12.377
nine,

01:01:13.002 --> 01:01:13.878
ten.

01:01:13.961 --> 01:01:15.088
TIME SPENT

01:01:15.171 --> 01:01:17.340
LEE CHANG-HO 4 HOURS 50 MINUTES
CHO HOON-HYUN 5 HOURS

01:01:17.423 --> 01:01:19.717
Cho 9-dan,
you have two byoyomi left.

01:02:31.205 --> 01:02:33.416
I don't know.
We'll know when it ends.

01:02:33.499 --> 01:02:35.835
-If this goes right…
-Huh?

01:02:35.918 --> 01:02:38.337
…we might see a real coup here.

01:02:38.421 --> 01:02:39.338
A coup d'état?

01:02:40.089 --> 01:02:41.716
-Really?
-Coup d'état?

01:02:42.717 --> 01:02:45.094
Oh, let's not do this.
Let's go see for ourselves.

01:02:45.178 --> 01:02:47.096
Hurry up! Hurry!

01:02:47.180 --> 01:02:48.931
-Run! Run! Run!
-What's going on?

01:02:49.599 --> 01:02:51.517
Let me see! Let me see!

01:02:51.601 --> 01:02:53.019
Let me see! Let me see!

01:02:55.146 --> 01:02:57.523
Quiet.

01:03:08.826 --> 01:03:09.911
Is it done?

01:03:33.100 --> 01:03:34.811
Black wins by half a point!

01:03:34.894 --> 01:03:36.729
At 271 moves!

01:03:36.813 --> 01:03:38.815
Hey, no, I said black.

01:03:38.898 --> 01:03:41.984
Listen! It's Lee Chang-ho that won!

01:04:01.170 --> 01:04:04.841
Um, it's so late.
The restaurants will be closing soon.

01:04:07.301 --> 01:04:08.636
-Champion Cho.
-Huh?

01:04:18.521 --> 01:04:20.481
A word for your student, and his victory?

01:04:20.565 --> 01:04:22.233
Champion Cho, can I get a comment?

01:04:26.904 --> 01:04:30.116
I've got nothing more to teach him.

01:04:30.199 --> 01:04:32.285
He can go his own way now.

01:04:32.368 --> 01:04:34.245
Where do you think the match went wrong?

01:04:34.328 --> 01:04:35.997
-Excuse me.
-Uh, Champion Cho!

01:04:36.080 --> 01:04:38.416
You'll likely face Lee 4-dan
in the Kisei too.

01:04:38.499 --> 01:04:41.460
How do you plan to prepare for that match,
Champion Cho?

01:04:49.886 --> 01:04:52.388
First of all, congratulations.
How are you feeling?

01:04:53.639 --> 01:04:55.224
I'm sorry to my seonsaengnim…

01:04:56.851 --> 01:04:58.352
I won with a bad game.

01:05:50.571 --> 01:05:51.906
You're late.

01:05:55.701 --> 01:05:56.953
How did it go?

01:06:09.340 --> 01:06:10.967
Chang-ho, you did so well.

01:06:11.509 --> 01:06:12.385
Congrats.

01:06:13.511 --> 01:06:14.470
Thank you, Auntie.

01:06:15.179 --> 01:06:16.931
Yes, good work, all right?

01:06:17.515 --> 01:06:19.767
You must be exhausted. Go rest.

01:06:19.850 --> 01:06:20.810
Okay.

01:06:31.195 --> 01:06:32.405
Grandpa.

01:06:33.823 --> 01:06:35.324
Did you see me win today?

01:06:37.618 --> 01:06:38.703
You know, I…

01:06:39.996 --> 01:06:41.747
wanted to win so much.

01:06:44.333 --> 01:06:45.626
Through my own style.

01:07:24.957 --> 01:07:26.667
A HALF-POINT WIN
SENSATION IN THE WORLD OF GO

01:07:26.751 --> 01:07:27.918
YOUNGEST CHAMP, LEE CHANG-HO

01:07:29.754 --> 01:07:31.213
That boy, well…

01:08:03.370 --> 01:08:04.872
Should I have wedged it?

01:08:19.970 --> 01:08:20.805
Oh.

01:08:21.305 --> 01:08:22.389
Seonsaengnim.

01:08:24.517 --> 01:08:26.143
Um, our review?

01:08:27.436 --> 01:08:28.771
Oh, yes. We should.

01:08:30.481 --> 01:08:33.359
Weather's good. Let's go out there.

01:08:37.488 --> 01:08:40.658
What if I defend right here?

01:08:41.242 --> 01:08:42.660
That's not bad either,

01:08:45.830 --> 01:08:47.039
but here is better…

01:08:51.210 --> 01:08:53.587
…and expand the center.

01:08:53.671 --> 01:08:54.713
The black's heavy.

01:09:01.762 --> 01:09:02.721
Or maybe…

01:09:06.809 --> 01:09:08.602
if I wedge it like this?

01:09:14.400 --> 01:09:15.317
Mmm…

01:09:18.028 --> 01:09:19.572
Uh…

01:09:22.491 --> 01:09:25.786
Hmm. That shape doesn't look good there.

01:09:26.412 --> 01:09:29.498
You could defend this side instead. Here.

01:09:29.582 --> 01:09:32.668
Or maybe attach it over here first.

01:09:35.045 --> 01:09:38.757
I don't think this is bad right here.

01:09:38.841 --> 01:09:42.094
We could do atari here, push through,

01:09:44.263 --> 01:09:45.222
and attach.

01:09:45.306 --> 01:09:48.225
No, not there. It's going
to leave a bad aftertaste.

01:09:49.518 --> 01:09:51.437
And no need to look further here.

01:09:55.816 --> 01:09:56.692
Seonsaengnim.

01:10:02.823 --> 01:10:03.824
I'm sorry.

01:10:04.742 --> 01:10:07.161
About yesterday.

01:10:09.455 --> 01:10:10.289
What?

01:10:14.501 --> 01:10:16.295
When I'm across the board.

01:10:18.339 --> 01:10:20.090
Am I seonsaengnim to you?

01:10:21.842 --> 01:10:23.010
Uh, no.

01:10:24.762 --> 01:10:25.679
You're my enemy.

01:10:25.763 --> 01:10:28.224
Winning a game doesn't mean
the world has changed.

01:10:29.600 --> 01:10:30.935
Don't become deluded.

01:10:31.602 --> 01:10:34.605
Go professionals win and lose every day,
and that's our fate.

01:10:34.688 --> 01:10:35.689
Arrogant punk.

01:10:37.900 --> 01:10:40.778
From now on, let's not review
games we've played.

01:11:27.616 --> 01:11:29.660
FOURTH KISEI CHALLENGE MATCH
LAST ROUND

01:11:29.743 --> 01:11:32.288
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 6-DAN

01:11:32.371 --> 01:11:34.665
It's the 27th game between them.

01:11:34.748 --> 01:11:36.375
It's a world-shaking event

01:11:36.458 --> 01:11:38.919
that will go down in Korean Go history.

01:11:39.003 --> 01:11:40.587
It's unprecedented.

01:11:40.671 --> 01:11:43.257
Yes. The Daewang, the Kisei,

01:11:43.340 --> 01:11:47.303
the Paewang, the Choegowi,
and now, Kiwang.

01:11:47.386 --> 01:11:51.390
The student and the teacher are meeting
for the finals of all five cups.

01:11:51.473 --> 01:11:54.184
This is all
because of Lee Chang-ho 6-dan.

01:11:54.268 --> 01:11:55.811
He's moving so quickly.

01:11:55.894 --> 01:11:58.814
Cho 9-dan probably didn't expect him
to rise so quickly, either.

01:11:58.897 --> 01:12:02.693
Recent games have shown
Cho 9-dan backed into a corner.

01:12:02.776 --> 01:12:05.904
Cho 9-dan's knife
is famous for its sharpness.

01:12:05.988 --> 01:12:07.990
It penetrates your weak spots mercilessly.

01:12:08.574 --> 01:12:09.575
But it seems

01:12:10.242 --> 01:12:12.369
it's not working on Lee Chang-ho 6-dan.

01:12:12.995 --> 01:12:16.790
Yes, Mr. Lee 6-dan lets
his opponents do as they like.

01:12:16.874 --> 01:12:19.918
But, when they're done,
and they realize they've lost,

01:12:20.002 --> 01:12:21.837
it leaves them dumbstruck.

01:12:21.920 --> 01:12:26.216
One professional player told me
he's scared to face Cho 9-dan.

01:12:26.300 --> 01:12:29.803
As for Chang-ho,
he doesn't even want to look at him.

01:12:29.887 --> 01:12:33.891
As everyone knows, the two
have completely different styles of play.

01:12:33.974 --> 01:12:35.893
The teacher is fast,
and the student is slow.

01:12:35.976 --> 01:12:38.395
The student holds, and the teacher fights.

01:12:39.063 --> 01:12:41.148
Looking only at recent games,

01:12:41.231 --> 01:12:44.109
they seem to have switched their styles.

01:12:44.193 --> 01:12:47.446
It is now the teacher who's on the defense

01:12:48.030 --> 01:12:49.990
while the student is on the offense.

01:12:50.074 --> 01:12:54.203
Cho 9-dan must be struggling
immensely to change this trend.

01:12:54.286 --> 01:12:58.248
I agree, but the problem is,
Lee Chang-ho isn't just good at defense.

01:12:58.999 --> 01:13:01.168
He was absolutely ruthless yesterday.

01:13:01.752 --> 01:13:05.756
Cho Hoon-hyun, Go's best,
hasn't once extended his hand.

01:13:05.839 --> 01:13:08.592
-Could I have a comment?
-Cho 9-dan!

01:13:08.675 --> 01:13:10.761
-Sir! Sir!
-Cho 9-dan!

01:13:10.844 --> 01:13:12.930
Lee 6-dan,
first of all, congratulations.

01:13:13.013 --> 01:13:15.057
Could you tell us how you're feeling?

01:13:17.393 --> 01:13:19.978
There's only
the Paewang left now.

01:13:20.062 --> 01:13:24.191
If Cho 9-dan loses there,
he'll have won no cups.

01:13:24.274 --> 01:13:25.109
GO SPECIAL FORUM

01:13:25.192 --> 01:13:28.904
So how do you all think that
the next upcoming game will go?

01:13:28.987 --> 01:13:30.906
Lee Chang-ho is in great spirits,

01:13:31.448 --> 01:13:33.951
but this is Cho Hoon-hyun, the King of Go.

01:13:34.034 --> 01:13:35.702
You can see
he won't back down easily here.

01:13:35.786 --> 01:13:37.204
Yes, that's right.

01:13:37.287 --> 01:13:39.623
Mr. Fujisawa 9-dan of Japan,

01:13:39.706 --> 01:13:42.751
this man won himself a cup
when he was well into his sixties.

01:13:42.835 --> 01:13:44.837
Oh, let's not be daft here.

01:13:46.004 --> 01:13:47.881
There wasn't a Lee Chang-ho in Japan!

01:13:47.965 --> 01:13:50.050
WINS THE YING SHIBEI CUP!
UNIFIES THE WORLD!

01:13:54.304 --> 01:13:55.973
Lee Chang-ho is changing
the paradigm of Go.

01:13:56.056 --> 01:13:57.724
LEE CHANG-HO, NEW STYLE OF PLAY AND MOVES

01:13:57.808 --> 01:13:59.643
This is what the fans of Go are saying.

01:13:59.726 --> 01:14:04.356
Go is a sport where you can fight all day,
only for Lee Chang-ho to win in the end.

01:14:07.317 --> 01:14:10.404
ETERNAL KINGDOM FALLEN BY HALF-POINT
CHO ON THE EDGE OF A CLIFF

01:14:10.487 --> 01:14:12.614
29TH PAEWANG CHALLENGE MATCH
FOURTH ROUND

01:14:12.698 --> 01:14:15.284
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 6-DAN

01:14:49.610 --> 01:14:51.278
-Oh.
-Champion Cho!

01:14:51.778 --> 01:14:53.906
-Over there, tissue. Please, tissue.
-Oh.

01:15:08.170 --> 01:15:11.298
Cho seonsaengnim. We'll be heading out.

01:15:11.882 --> 01:15:14.510
Oh, yes. Have a safe trip home.

01:15:23.769 --> 01:15:26.271
Terrible situation.

01:15:27.731 --> 01:15:29.316
For you and for Chang-ho.

01:15:51.296 --> 01:15:52.464
Stomach bothering you?

01:15:56.385 --> 01:15:57.511
I feel awful.

01:15:59.179 --> 01:16:00.806
For my seonsaengnim, you know.

01:16:03.267 --> 01:16:04.518
Also for my Auntie.

01:16:07.813 --> 01:16:08.689
Well…

01:16:10.357 --> 01:16:11.900
would you rather lose?

01:16:19.199 --> 01:16:20.826
Then give it your best and win.

01:16:22.202 --> 01:16:23.704
What else can you do?

01:16:57.779 --> 01:16:59.531
You're back?

01:17:10.876 --> 01:17:13.045
There was a time
you couldn't tie your shoes,

01:17:13.545 --> 01:17:16.381
but now you're a professional.

01:17:23.764 --> 01:17:24.765
It's time

01:17:27.100 --> 01:17:28.518
for you to stand alone.

01:17:30.562 --> 01:17:32.481
You've surpassed me already.

01:17:34.149 --> 01:17:36.693
It makes no sense
to keep you as my student.

01:17:38.445 --> 01:17:39.571
I'm not there yet.

01:17:39.655 --> 01:17:42.699
There's still so much I don't know
that I should be learning from you.

01:17:42.783 --> 01:17:45.327
Well, not from me.

01:17:48.914 --> 01:17:51.416
I really should have sent you away
much sooner.

01:17:56.129 --> 01:17:58.715
Though winning and losing
is a part of our lives,

01:18:01.385 --> 01:18:03.387
it's been hard for both of us,

01:18:05.263 --> 01:18:06.932
living in the same house,

01:18:09.059 --> 01:18:10.394
fighting across the board.

01:18:12.312 --> 01:18:14.314
I'm sorry, seonsaengnim.

01:18:16.316 --> 01:18:17.359
I didn't teach you that.

01:18:19.945 --> 01:18:23.448
The pro's job is to win,
no matter the opponent.

01:18:31.832 --> 01:18:34.042
You've taught me a lot
these days, as well.

01:18:35.752 --> 01:18:38.004
I'm learning
that I can lose at any time, now.

01:18:46.096 --> 01:18:47.431
You'll do fine without me,

01:18:48.890 --> 01:18:50.642
but after you leave, don't be lazy.

01:19:05.782 --> 01:19:07.033
Thinking about it,

01:19:08.910 --> 01:19:13.623
I never once complimented you
in all this time you've been here with us.

01:19:16.918 --> 01:19:18.170
Your seonsaengnim…

01:19:21.047 --> 01:19:22.799
has always been very proud of you.

01:19:25.761 --> 01:19:26.762
You were…

01:19:29.389 --> 01:19:30.515
always my pride.

01:19:50.243 --> 01:19:52.037
Here's yeolmu kimchi for you.

01:19:52.537 --> 01:19:53.705
Uh, Chang-ho really likes it.

01:19:53.789 --> 01:19:55.290
Oh, thank you.

01:19:56.374 --> 01:19:57.375
Okay, we're done.

01:19:59.419 --> 01:20:00.420
Chang-ho.

01:20:01.338 --> 01:20:02.714
Let me have a big hug.

01:20:03.965 --> 01:20:06.927
Eat well, okay? Come visit us too.

01:20:09.346 --> 01:20:10.889
I will. Thanks, Auntie.

01:20:18.939 --> 01:20:22.943
Dress warmly.
Come by for side dishes when you run out.

01:20:23.026 --> 01:20:24.903
Sir, thank you so much
for everything.

01:20:25.529 --> 01:20:26.571
It was nothing.

01:20:26.655 --> 01:20:27.989
Please, be well.

01:20:28.073 --> 01:20:30.408
Yes, you too. Have a safe journey.

01:20:33.995 --> 01:20:34.996
Seonsaengnim.

01:20:42.170 --> 01:20:45.048
Thank you so much for everything.

01:20:45.757 --> 01:20:47.092
Oh…

01:20:57.102 --> 01:20:59.646
Your seonsaengnim gave this to you.

01:21:16.621 --> 01:21:18.415
WHITE CHO HYEON-SIK VS BLACK LEE CHANG-HO

01:21:18.498 --> 01:21:19.499
BLACK WINS BY 1.5 POINTS

01:21:59.372 --> 01:22:01.750
The Great Cho Hoon-hyun
without a single cup.

01:22:01.833 --> 01:22:05.337
He's getting devoured
by the tiger cub he raised.

01:22:05.420 --> 01:22:06.671
Who can he blame?

01:22:06.755 --> 01:22:08.298
Still, it must sting.

01:22:08.381 --> 01:22:13.053
Yeah, we make more money when the matches
are basically neck-and-neck,

01:22:13.136 --> 01:22:16.264
and not like this, huh?
We won't make much commission this way.

01:22:17.098 --> 01:22:19.684
On Chang-ho, let's lower the payout.

01:22:21.102 --> 01:22:25.899
One, two, three, four, five…

01:22:25.982 --> 01:22:28.777
19TH KIWANG FINALS
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS NAM GI-CHEOL 9-DAN

01:22:28.902 --> 01:22:31.279
…six, seven, eight, nine, ten.

01:22:33.448 --> 01:22:35.283
Cho 9-dan, runs out of time.

01:22:36.076 --> 01:22:38.286
Nam 9-dan wins by default.

01:23:06.648 --> 01:23:07.524
The kids?

01:23:08.441 --> 01:23:10.235
-Not home yet?
-Mm-mm.

01:23:11.528 --> 01:23:12.612
How was the game?

01:23:14.030 --> 01:23:15.198
I lost.

01:23:16.366 --> 01:23:18.159
I'll live with you if you lose…

01:23:19.369 --> 01:23:20.745
but not if you're pathetic.

01:23:21.788 --> 01:23:24.332
Stop running from what's real.

01:23:27.335 --> 01:23:28.795
I never resented either of you

01:23:29.754 --> 01:23:32.507
during all of those years
we took care of Chang-ho.

01:23:34.050 --> 01:23:35.552
But seeing you like this…

01:23:36.720 --> 01:23:38.138
I'm resenting him now.

01:23:40.807 --> 01:23:42.726
Don't be pathetic.

01:23:49.482 --> 01:23:50.358
Ah.

01:23:51.526 --> 01:23:54.404
Oh. Hey, Champion Lee,
it's been a long time!

01:23:54.487 --> 01:23:55.363
You eat?

01:23:55.864 --> 01:23:58.199
Well, if you didn't,
let's go get something.

01:23:58.283 --> 01:24:00.744
No thanks, I'm not really hungry yet.

01:24:00.827 --> 01:24:02.328
I'm sure he's full.

01:24:02.412 --> 01:24:05.540
He's gorged himself
on all those championship titles,

01:24:05.623 --> 01:24:07.584
and devoured his seonsaengnim.

01:24:07.667 --> 01:24:10.336
Hey, what do you mean he devoured him?
You take that back.

01:24:10.420 --> 01:24:12.839
Why are you getting so upset?

01:24:14.340 --> 01:24:15.759
Why don't you laugh?

01:24:15.842 --> 01:24:16.801
It's a joke.

01:24:20.346 --> 01:24:23.516
Oh, it must be nice, Pro Lee, huh?
Wow. You're photogenic too.

01:24:23.600 --> 01:24:25.435
THE STUDENT WHO STABBED
THE TEACHER IN THE BACK

01:24:25.518 --> 01:24:27.103
ANOTHER FORFEIT
WILL CHO HOON-HYUN RETIRE?

01:24:27.937 --> 01:24:30.482
Wow, you could be a model, really.

01:24:34.319 --> 01:24:37.072
Why don't we have intestine soup?

01:24:37.155 --> 01:24:38.573
-It's been a while.
-Mmm, okay.

01:24:38.656 --> 01:24:41.534
-How about a drink to go with it?
-Well, then what should I do?

01:24:46.456 --> 01:24:47.290
Huh?

01:24:48.208 --> 01:24:50.835
Pro Baek, if you were me,
what would you do?

01:24:52.295 --> 01:24:53.755
Should I just lose?

01:24:54.464 --> 01:24:57.217
Hey.
What are you asking me for?

01:24:58.468 --> 01:25:03.431
That's what I was taught.
That a pro's job is to win.

01:25:05.308 --> 01:25:08.645
You must not have ever met a good teacher
to learn from yet, Pro Baek.

01:25:08.728 --> 01:25:10.021
You're such a…

01:25:11.356 --> 01:25:13.108
Your mouth is getting ahead of you now.

01:25:14.859 --> 01:25:15.985
You're not laughing.

01:25:17.028 --> 01:25:18.571
I was joking a bit, too.

01:25:18.655 --> 01:25:19.864
What?

01:25:21.533 --> 01:25:23.451
A joke. He's joking.

01:25:24.077 --> 01:25:25.787
Champion Lee, let's go. Come on.

01:25:31.876 --> 01:25:34.295
A forfeit? The Great Cho Hoon-hyun?

01:25:34.879 --> 01:25:37.298
-You should have at least shown up!
-Hmm.

01:25:37.382 --> 01:25:39.717
Do you know how much
your wife worries about you?

01:25:41.052 --> 01:25:42.053
And Chang-ho?

01:25:42.762 --> 01:25:44.055
He doesn't talk about it,

01:25:44.889 --> 01:25:47.433
but think of how uncomfortable this is
for him as well.

01:25:55.400 --> 01:25:58.153
Hey, what are you doing that for?
You're a lightweight.

01:26:01.114 --> 01:26:02.657
Hey, Champion Cho.

01:26:03.741 --> 01:26:04.576
Huh?

01:26:15.044 --> 01:26:16.713
My knife's rusted.

01:26:21.551 --> 01:26:23.553
Hold on. You don't have an umbrella.

01:26:23.636 --> 01:26:25.013
Hey, Champion Cho!

01:27:11.893 --> 01:27:14.229
CHO HOON-HYUN VS LEE CHANG-HO
NO-COUNT WIN BY LEE

01:27:30.453 --> 01:27:33.581
I'd be upset if you bowed down
to something as small as this.

01:27:36.125 --> 01:27:39.337
You have stabbed me
at least a hundred times now, in my back.

01:27:42.674 --> 01:27:44.759
Everyone hurts when they've been punched.

01:27:45.843 --> 01:27:48.346
Chang-ho must have it hard.

01:27:50.807 --> 01:27:52.350
The poor kid's suffering.

01:27:53.768 --> 01:27:55.353
He met the wrong teacher.

01:27:57.063 --> 01:28:00.275
He can't even try to laugh
even while he's winning.

01:28:01.776 --> 01:28:03.569
He's not done learning from you.

01:28:05.405 --> 01:28:08.408
You need to challenge him,
so that he'll grow stronger.

01:28:11.077 --> 01:28:12.787
The game of Go is so odd.

01:28:15.456 --> 01:28:16.874
Once you place a stone,

01:28:18.251 --> 01:28:19.961
you feel like you can do it,

01:28:22.255 --> 01:28:24.173
but the first stone is the hardest.

01:28:28.761 --> 01:28:31.264
I thought
I understood the game, but…

01:28:33.725 --> 01:28:35.643
You have to endure that, to win.

01:28:37.603 --> 01:28:41.441
The wound oozes, scabs over,
and then new flesh covers the wound.

01:28:43.109 --> 01:28:44.360
You keep biting down,

01:28:47.113 --> 01:28:48.740
and you'll find an opportunity.

01:28:52.285 --> 01:28:53.578
Champion Cho.

01:28:56.080 --> 01:28:58.583
Once you start avoiding
your opponent on the board,

01:29:01.627 --> 01:29:03.254
there's nowhere left to go.

01:29:15.224 --> 01:29:16.517
Act like yourself.

01:29:17.894 --> 01:29:19.437
Being small and quiet

01:29:21.189 --> 01:29:22.607
does not suit you at all.

01:30:06.150 --> 01:30:09.028
GO IS ABOUT TRYING TO FIND AN ANSWER
WHEN THERE ARE NO ANSWERS

01:30:09.112 --> 01:30:10.905
SEGOE KENSAKU (CHO HOON-HYUN'S MASTER)

01:30:32.802 --> 01:30:37.640
GO IS A FIGHT AGAINST YOURSELF
JULY 1964, CHO HOON-HYUN

01:30:41.352 --> 01:30:43.938
Oh, I'm full. That was great.

01:30:44.021 --> 01:30:46.190
Pro Baek, early congrats on your win.

01:30:46.274 --> 01:30:48.151
I didn't see Champion Cho today.

01:30:48.234 --> 01:30:51.070
Don't congratulate me. This leaves
a bad taste even when I win.

01:30:51.154 --> 01:30:55.116
Ugh, now's the moment to face off
against Cho Hoon-hyun and crush him.

01:30:56.492 --> 01:30:58.661
-He's scared and lost his nerve.
-He's off the deep end.

01:31:02.832 --> 01:31:05.293
Oh, Pro Baek, you've arrived.

01:31:06.043 --> 01:31:07.044
So,

01:31:08.129 --> 01:31:09.589
have you had a good meal, sir?

01:31:13.217 --> 01:31:18.055
ONE YEAR LATER

01:31:22.977 --> 01:31:25.062
SECOND WOMEN'S GUKSU CUP FINALS

01:31:25.146 --> 01:31:26.606
Huh? Seonsaengnim.

01:31:27.607 --> 01:31:30.067
Oh, you. Hey, let me help you with that.

01:31:30.151 --> 01:31:32.904
Oh, no, it's okay. I'll do it.

01:31:42.538 --> 01:31:43.456
Seonsaengnim.

01:31:45.124 --> 01:31:46.167
Today's game…

01:31:47.084 --> 01:31:49.462
You're embarrassing. Wow.

01:31:49.962 --> 01:31:52.465
Punk, I won. Oh man.

01:31:54.258 --> 01:31:57.428
Aigo! Look at me, in the preliminaries.

01:31:59.430 --> 01:32:01.224
I saw your latest game.

01:32:02.141 --> 01:32:05.144
You still won't put up a fight, will you?

01:32:06.270 --> 01:32:08.397
Because I can win without fighting.

01:32:09.941 --> 01:32:13.361
So why should I risk it by fighting?

01:32:13.861 --> 01:32:17.073
You're not avoiding that
because you're fearful?

01:32:17.156 --> 01:32:18.616
Of course I'm not.

01:32:19.534 --> 01:32:21.327
Whose student am I, huh?

01:32:25.957 --> 01:32:29.252
Yeah. Well, look at me
lecturing to a higher player.

01:32:31.462 --> 01:32:34.090
Lee Chang-ho 7-dan
wins a no-count win

01:32:34.173 --> 01:32:36.384
and succeeds defending his title
of Daewang.

01:32:36.467 --> 01:32:39.095
He has 19 consecutive competition wins…

01:32:39.178 --> 01:32:43.516
What matters is how many consecutive wins
Lee Chang-ho gets, you know what I mean?

01:32:43.599 --> 01:32:45.601
The Paewang will be held in 15 days…

01:32:45.685 --> 01:32:49.063
You don't have to watch
to know Lee will win three to zero.

01:32:49.146 --> 01:32:51.607
Cho Hoon-hyun is a has-been now.

01:32:51.691 --> 01:32:53.776
Cho 9-dan,
who's been going through a slump

01:32:53.859 --> 01:32:56.112
won through a variety
of preliminaries and finals,

01:32:56.195 --> 01:32:58.948
and now will challenge
Lee 7-dan once again.

01:32:59.031 --> 01:33:00.116
Lee 7-dan…

01:33:02.910 --> 01:33:04.495
-Hello.
-You're here.

01:33:04.579 --> 01:33:05.997
-We're all done.
-Okay.

01:33:06.539 --> 01:33:08.457
-Hey, he's all mic'd up, yes?
-Yes.

01:33:10.042 --> 01:33:13.045
Champion Cho.
You can skip this if you want you.

01:33:13.963 --> 01:33:14.797
Should I?

01:33:15.881 --> 01:33:18.884
-Huh?
-I'm joking.

01:33:18.968 --> 01:33:21.637
It's time I did one. It's been a while.

01:33:22.305 --> 01:33:23.723
Come on.

01:33:26.183 --> 01:33:27.768
First of all, congratulations.

01:33:27.852 --> 01:33:32.106
You were voted
the most popular Go player…

01:33:32.189 --> 01:33:33.149
…by the fans.

01:33:33.232 --> 01:33:34.233
How do you feel about it?

01:33:34.317 --> 01:33:38.613
If I knew it'd be like this,
I would have lost much sooner.

01:33:38.696 --> 01:33:41.407
When I was champion, I was hated so much.

01:33:43.200 --> 01:33:48.831
Well, the records show
you've played 110 matches last year alone.

01:33:48.914 --> 01:33:51.917
You've been playing practically
once every three days,

01:33:52.001 --> 01:33:54.920
including all the preliminaries
and the finals.

01:33:55.004 --> 01:33:58.591
In the past, you must have gotten used
to waiting as the defending champion.

01:33:59.300 --> 01:34:00.259
It's been rough.

01:34:02.386 --> 01:34:06.766
Although, it makes the match
more exhilarating when a single…

01:34:06.849 --> 01:34:09.644
…loss could send
you down that cliff.

01:34:09.727 --> 01:34:10.978
Fun, in a way.

01:34:11.062 --> 01:34:13.689
It was refreshing going
against those young rookies too.

01:34:16.150 --> 01:34:18.569
Lately, Lee Chang-ho 7-dan is on a roll.

01:34:18.653 --> 01:34:21.447
They say you're not a professional
until you lose to him.

01:34:21.530 --> 01:34:23.824
Let's end the interview
with your intentions.

01:34:24.367 --> 01:34:28.663
Any messages for Lee 7-dan,
your student and opponent in the final?

01:34:34.085 --> 01:34:37.046
Ah, Lee Chang-ho, he's my opponent.

01:34:39.006 --> 01:34:41.759
And even if I have to go against him,

01:34:42.635 --> 01:34:44.637
I plan on giving it my absolute best.

01:34:45.221 --> 01:34:49.308
It's now my turn
to challenge him as he once did me.

01:34:58.401 --> 01:34:59.652
CHO HOON-HYUN RETURNS!

01:35:24.593 --> 01:35:27.596
31ST PAEWANG CUP CHALLENGE MATCH
LAST ROUND

01:35:27.680 --> 01:35:30.141
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 7-DAN

01:35:52.121 --> 01:35:55.166
This is the final game,
and both sides have two wins each,

01:35:55.249 --> 01:35:57.418
I was thinking the game
would begin in a cautious manner,

01:35:57.501 --> 01:36:00.212
but it's going extremely quickly,

01:36:00.296 --> 01:36:04.216
and the opening so far
is the same as the fourth match.

01:36:04.300 --> 01:36:05.801
Like they've choreographed their moves.

01:36:05.885 --> 01:36:08.679
It's very heated,
with neither of them backing down.

01:36:09.221 --> 01:36:11.849
They're both shouting
their way of Go is correct.

01:36:11.932 --> 01:36:16.228
Lee Chang-ho 7-dan
is known as "The God of Calculation."

01:36:16.312 --> 01:36:20.316
Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan won
the very first two matches

01:36:20.399 --> 01:36:24.570
but lost the next two, and is now
standing at the edge of a cliff.

01:36:24.653 --> 01:36:28.199
The matches between the once student
and teacher continue in this pattern,

01:36:28.282 --> 01:36:32.036
with comeback wins now a signature
of Lee Chang-ho 7-dan's.

01:36:32.119 --> 01:36:36.957
Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan's challenge
is to keep his composure 'til the end.

01:36:43.672 --> 01:36:45.090
Cho 9-dan's interesting.

01:36:45.674 --> 01:36:48.385
It's customary to take
and strengthen right here.

01:36:48.469 --> 01:36:50.679
Cho 9-dan placed his stone here.

01:36:51.388 --> 01:36:54.558
Hasn't Cho 9-dan's Go become
much sharper and acute

01:36:54.642 --> 01:36:56.769
since he's bounced back
from hitting rock bottom?

01:36:56.852 --> 01:37:00.189
His new nickname is "The God of War."

01:37:00.272 --> 01:37:04.568
From that perspective, it seems
Cho 9-dan is planning to incite a fight.

01:37:05.152 --> 01:37:06.904
How will Lee 7-dan respond?

01:37:08.697 --> 01:37:11.659
Oh, Lee 7-dan makes a hit!

01:37:11.742 --> 01:37:13.118
He's capturing.

01:37:13.202 --> 01:37:17.122
He doesn't seem to have any intention
to compromise. Unusual.

01:37:17.206 --> 01:37:19.667
It doesn't seem Cho 9-dan
expected this either.

01:37:37.852 --> 01:37:42.439
Lee Chang-ho 7-dan strikes back
against Cho 9-dan's wave of attacks.

01:37:45.276 --> 01:37:47.027
Cho 9-dan shakes up the center.

01:37:47.945 --> 01:37:51.073
It doesn't seem like Lee Chang-ho
will have to rise to the attack.

01:37:54.994 --> 01:37:58.455
Wow, Lee Chang-ho jumping in!

01:37:59.081 --> 01:38:01.667
They don't dare move their eyes
from the board.

01:38:01.750 --> 01:38:03.919
All they care about is the battle!

01:38:04.628 --> 01:38:06.922
Neither the teacher nor the student

01:38:07.006 --> 01:38:10.301
will give an inch
when it comes to the match.

01:38:24.690 --> 01:38:26.734
This battle is truly chilling.

01:38:27.276 --> 01:38:29.737
They're fighting
like they're mortal enemies.

01:38:33.908 --> 01:38:36.911
Lee Chang-ho 7-dan is deep in thought.

01:38:37.578 --> 01:38:42.082
He's probably running tens of thousands
of possible sequences in his head.

01:39:04.229 --> 01:39:07.149
Oh, Lee Chang-ho suddenly
makes a sharp jab.

01:39:07.733 --> 01:39:09.902
Cho 9-dan has to be aching.

01:39:10.945 --> 01:39:14.281
Overall, the white
seems to be at an advantage.

01:39:14.365 --> 01:39:16.158
What are you thinking, Nam 9-dan?

01:39:16.241 --> 01:39:19.620
Champion Cho is starting fights
here and there,

01:39:20.788 --> 01:39:22.748
but Chan-ho's walls are just too thick.

01:39:22.831 --> 01:39:25.125
It seems
Lee Chang-ho 7-dan is ahead

01:39:25.209 --> 01:39:28.462
by three and a half
or four and a half points so far.

01:39:28.545 --> 01:39:32.967
Yes. This intense match
is entering its final endgame.

01:39:33.509 --> 01:39:35.886
If Lee Chang-ho 7-dan wins today,

01:39:35.970 --> 01:39:39.682
he'll become the second winner
of all cups, following his teacher.

01:39:39.765 --> 01:39:42.685
Lee Chang-ho 7-dan is almost there.

01:39:47.606 --> 01:39:50.985
Oh, is he making a counterattack
in this situation?

01:39:51.527 --> 01:39:54.321
Is Cho 9-dan planning
to capture in this area?

01:39:54.405 --> 01:39:56.407
It won't be easy.

01:39:56.907 --> 01:39:59.493
It's Lee Chang-ho he's facing, after all.

01:40:00.202 --> 01:40:01.662
His defense is strong.

01:40:01.745 --> 01:40:03.956
It's Lee Chang-ho. A good position?

01:40:04.039 --> 01:40:07.626
Oh yes, he's staged a defense
and attacked a vital spot.

01:40:08.669 --> 01:40:11.213
It's very Lee Chang-ho.

01:40:13.173 --> 01:40:14.967
Cho 9-dan
is now on the defensive.

01:40:15.050 --> 01:40:17.720
How will he get out
of this difficult situation?

01:40:18.887 --> 01:40:22.808
Cho 9-dan has never once been
at an advantage during this game.

01:40:36.947 --> 01:40:40.409
Oh, what was that move?
Did that make any sense?

01:40:40.492 --> 01:40:43.162
What?
He's going to jump more here?

01:40:43.245 --> 01:40:45.456
Whoa, it's too reckless.

01:40:45.539 --> 01:40:47.291
There is nothing supporting it.

01:40:58.177 --> 01:41:00.804
Oh, Lee Chang-oh 7-dan retreated.

01:41:01.638 --> 01:41:06.143
I think it'd be better to bend here
and capture one point, instead, right?

01:41:06.935 --> 01:41:08.103
What does that do?

01:41:10.272 --> 01:41:13.901
Is there perhaps something more
to Cho 9-dan's move?

01:41:15.027 --> 01:41:15.986
I'm perplexed.

01:41:16.070 --> 01:41:19.073
What are they up to?
There's something else going on.

01:41:23.869 --> 01:41:26.705
Vital points are painful.

01:41:28.916 --> 01:41:33.629
The points where once you get hit,
you can't move and can only gasp.

01:41:36.924 --> 01:41:38.926
More stones on the board mingling,

01:41:40.177 --> 01:41:41.720
result in more vital points.

01:41:43.639 --> 01:41:46.141
My vital point is

01:41:47.559 --> 01:41:49.061
my opponent's vital point.

01:41:52.564 --> 01:41:54.525
-Wait just a minute.
-Okay.

01:41:55.067 --> 01:41:56.652
I see it. It's complete genius.

01:41:57.528 --> 01:41:59.947
Black falls here, white does an atari,

01:42:00.030 --> 01:42:02.241
black connects,
then the white extends here.

01:42:02.825 --> 01:42:06.328
And in the end,
black inevitably gets the initiative.

01:42:06.411 --> 01:42:08.956
It's an exquisite victory bid
by Cho 9-dan.

01:42:09.039 --> 01:42:11.708
The teacher is finally twisting
the student's arm!

01:42:12.292 --> 01:42:15.754
If this works, Cho 9-dan
might actually turn the game around.

01:42:16.755 --> 01:42:18.382
It takes two to play Go.

01:42:19.967 --> 01:42:24.012
A single genius player can't create
a good game of Go by himself.

01:42:25.722 --> 01:42:29.560
This match
is one that will go down in history.

01:42:42.531 --> 01:42:44.658
Lee Chang-ho bends
on the left side.

01:42:45.617 --> 01:42:47.119
Cho 9-dan blocks decisively.

01:43:01.133 --> 01:43:04.136
Oh-oh-oh, the stone statue
just winced, oh my!

01:43:04.219 --> 01:43:06.221
Lee Chang-ho is human after all!

01:43:09.433 --> 01:43:10.267
Huh?

01:44:09.076 --> 01:44:10.702
Lee Chang-ho resigns!

01:44:10.786 --> 01:44:14.706
Cho Hoon-hyun just blocked
Lee Chang-ho from a grand slam!

01:44:14.790 --> 01:44:16.083
Cho Hoon-hyun has won!

01:44:16.792 --> 01:44:21.088
Cho Hoon-hyun, who rose again and again
after 15 losses,

01:44:21.171 --> 01:44:25.092
finally leaves the hellish tunnel
that is Lee Chang-ho!

01:44:26.134 --> 01:44:30.514
Cho 9-dan becomes the Paewang
and escapes champion title exile!

01:44:30.597 --> 01:44:32.307
Everyone!

01:44:32.391 --> 01:44:34.142
We welcome back the King!

01:45:21.273 --> 01:45:22.107
WINNER

01:45:32.868 --> 01:45:37.664
29TH PAEWANG CHALLENGE WINNER

01:45:46.298 --> 01:45:47.758
Have a safe journey back.

01:45:49.509 --> 01:45:50.594
Oh, here.

01:45:51.261 --> 01:45:52.095
Here, uh…

01:45:52.179 --> 01:45:54.598
Well, it didn't feel right
throwing it out.

01:45:54.681 --> 01:45:56.600
It's still usable. Here.

01:46:03.357 --> 01:46:04.733
TAXI

01:46:05.317 --> 01:46:09.321
Cut, throw-in, then bend,

01:46:10.197 --> 01:46:12.574
atari, then cover…

01:46:37.182 --> 01:46:39.101
GO IS FINDING AN ANSWER
WHEN THERE ARE NO ANSWERS

01:46:42.020 --> 01:46:46.525
GO IS A FIGHT AGAINST YOURSELF
JULY 1964, CHO HOON-HYUN

01:46:54.116 --> 01:46:58.829
NOVEMBER 16, 1998
42ND GUKSU CUP EVE EVENT

01:46:59.496 --> 01:47:01.206
Now,
let's wrap up the pictures

01:47:01.289 --> 01:47:02.707
and start the press conference.

01:47:02.791 --> 01:47:06.962
If the reporters could all please move
to their designated seats.

01:47:09.798 --> 01:47:14.386
First, the Guksu title has come
to represent you in a way,

01:47:14.469 --> 01:47:17.097
and so you must be feeling very emotional.

01:47:17.180 --> 01:47:18.306
You get a title,

01:47:19.516 --> 01:47:22.561
and can have it taken from you.
That's how it goes, right?

01:47:22.644 --> 01:47:24.271
Or it could be my age.

01:47:25.021 --> 01:47:28.066
But I'm more interested in…

01:47:29.818 --> 01:47:32.863
leaving behind a legacy game record
in my name.

01:47:32.946 --> 01:47:35.615
Cho 9-dan, you've been
on winning streak recently.

01:47:36.283 --> 01:47:37.993
What is your secret formula?

01:47:39.327 --> 01:47:40.495
Well…

01:47:41.955 --> 01:47:42.998
Uh…

01:47:43.081 --> 01:47:47.627
Well, don't they say
the, uh, sun shines the brightest

01:47:47.711 --> 01:47:50.046
right before it begins to set?

01:47:51.715 --> 01:47:54.968
I expect it will be subsiding
sometime soon.

01:47:55.051 --> 01:47:57.012
What's your take, Lee 9-dan ?

01:47:58.763 --> 01:48:01.475
He definitely stopped making
mistakes in the closing

01:48:01.558 --> 01:48:02.726
ever since he stopped smoking.

01:48:02.809 --> 01:48:04.519
Smoking must have been the problem.

01:48:05.854 --> 01:48:07.189
Ha! Thank you.

01:48:08.356 --> 01:48:13.278
Uh, finally, do either of you have
a map in your mind for tomorrow's match?

01:48:13.862 --> 01:48:14.696
Hmm…

01:48:16.281 --> 01:48:18.742
Chang-ho's gotten a taste
for comeback wins,

01:48:19.451 --> 01:48:21.328
so he let me have the first round,

01:48:22.787 --> 01:48:26.166
but now that we're going for it,
I'll make tomorrow's match a lesson.

01:48:29.002 --> 01:48:31.588
I think that the one match
was lesson enough.

01:48:33.548 --> 01:48:36.968
Many are rooting
for my seonsaengnim Cho's victory,

01:48:37.636 --> 01:48:43.141
though I am not planning to give him
the championship title so easily either.

01:49:07.791 --> 01:49:09.626
Chang-ho, you again?

01:49:12.379 --> 01:49:13.547
Yes, seonsaengnim.

01:49:18.134 --> 01:49:19.761
Ha, what can you do?

01:49:20.637 --> 01:49:22.055
This is the match.

01:49:29.104 --> 01:49:35.026
MUSHIM: TO EMPTY OUT ONE'S HEART

01:49:41.199 --> 01:49:47.122
SEONG-EUI: TO GIVE ALL ONE'S HEART

01:50:41.009 --> 01:50:41.843
NOVEMBER 17, 1998

01:50:41.926 --> 01:50:44.012
CHO HOON-HYUN TAKES BACK
THE GUKSU CHAMPION TITLE,

01:50:44.095 --> 01:50:46.222
WHICH WAS HIS SYMBOL,
FROM LEE CHANG-HO AFTER FIVE YEARS

01:50:46.306 --> 01:50:47.557
THE FIRST SNOW FELL THAT DAY

01:50:53.855 --> 01:50:56.650
LEE CHANG-HO RULED AT THE TOP
OF THE INTERNATIONAL GO SCENE FOR 15 YEARS

01:50:56.733 --> 01:50:58.026
FOLLOWING HIS TEACHER'S FOOTSTEPS

01:50:58.109 --> 01:51:00.362
AND IS STILL CONSIDERED
AS THE STRONGEST PLAYER IN HISTORY

01:51:04.407 --> 01:51:07.035
THE TEACHER AND THE STUDENT

01:51:07.118 --> 01:51:10.914
ARE STILL PLAYING
